UNWIND [{name:"Dharma Prabhu", properties:{entity_id:"Dharma Prabhu"}}, {name:"Paramatma", properties:{entity_id:"Paramatma"}}, {name:"Prarabdha", properties:{entity_id:"Prarabdha"}}, {name:"Mantra", properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oUCZWSi8zY4)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_XDcXdBDZ0c)<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hh61tFdyX8c)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=207izZBbqVg)<SEP>YouTube Video: M_BYTcsLQuY (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=M_BYTcsLQuY)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Mantra is a sacred utterance or sound, often described as a chant, a verbal affirmation, or a spiritual concept. It functions as a tool to silence the mind and reduce unnecessary thought chatter, and is used in meditation to aid concentration and foster spiritual connection. The repetitive structure of a mantra is likened to a chant recited during the state of Divine Inspiration, and it is also employed by the Tapatis in their practices to invoke divine presence.

The specific phrase ?I let go of the desperation of my small, limited self and allow the universal intelligence to take over my problem? is repeated three times during the practice, serving as a focal point for releasing desperation and inviting universal intelligence. This phrase underscores the mantra?s role in facilitating a shift from a limited self to a broader, universal perspective.

While most descriptions portray the mantra positively, one account notes that a mantra can become ?mangled,? suggesting an unintended disruption in its intended effect. This observation highlights that, despite its sacred nature, the mantra?s efficacy may be compromised if its structure or repetition is altered.

Mantra is a spiritual concept in yoga or philosophy, and is referenced in the text as being combined with dharana, which is a practice of concentration. It is also a concept referring to sacred utterances or sounds believed to hold spiritual power. In Hinduism, a mantra is a sacred utterance believed to have spiritual power when chanted correctly.

The mantra consists of a series of Sanskrit phrases and instructions, including ?Parvatim Parvapujitam...? and the directive to perform dharana. It is also a sacred<SEP>A mantra is a sacred word or phrase used in meditation to create vibrational energy, such as \"Aham Brahmasmi.\"", created_at:1779552769, source_id:"chunk-0f71ee987f163ec7e16a16625977c53b<SEP>chunk-1d93dc520a0588d5566528e75d99011c<SEP>chunk-e485856c846e316df06cb23fc5d1ca15<SEP>chunk-be9c73e40b66848f42c3e9def2b9ea2d<SEP>chunk-0f072682ae3f44593523bf73ac3ea68d<SEP>chunk-9656a8edd47ef08164c3565d2801af16<SEP>chunk-5bdd4af6edc5e8065c7f95fb8fc0543f<SEP>chunk-f4e31e3d7acd5226175acba9778623e9<SEP>chunk-fe04edafc045a28a3551d9aaa81cc514<SEP>chunk-e9d6a455cfecdcbfbf4b9187a0f8773c<SEP>chunk-242c86adb935c1461785f26c0c3f9e28<SEP>chunk-cdb6ddc2b47b984a3a935456e27dbbae<SEP>chunk-04853834df8aa59c8dac460b12fa6f79<SEP>chunk-ff46b53ab89c597d3fb954e4982613d0<SEP>chunk-6aebd99b80a116244470eacf183c4202<SEP>chunk-61c0437442c1a79367c1612c9b022b8f<SEP>chunk-8aa416f4b92bde5e908126e0e7ad0000", entity_id:"Mantra"}}, {name:"Dharma", properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: AyUE-2Uh5Vg (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AyUE-2Uh5Vg)<SEP>YouTube Video: 4LIZkNHlNaM (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4LIZkNHlNaM)<SEP>YouTube Video: aqSM9LwqWgA (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aqSM9LwqWgA)<SEP>YouTube Video: s6B81c2uTGg (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=s6B81c2uTGg)<SEP>YouTube Video: Xk1KsO3efP4 (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Xk1KsO3efP4)<SEP>YouTube Video: p2HecXyM3tE (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=p2HecXyM3tE)<SEP>YouTube Video: YkIBYppBtro (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YkIBYppBtro)<SEP>YouTube Video: ftFDBaH7RFg (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ftFDBaH7RFg)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BkM7IcqUaj0)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zGhlBQ8iWl4)", entity_type:"concept", truncate