Guru is a term with two primary meanings in Hindu tradition. First, it refers to a", source_id:"chunk-2e434306df5b4f2083250fff41e8b701<SEP>chunk-79727c38a2ca8d63adfca02ee83cd218<SEP>chunk-ed14675eaeee5b36e94642ad031a9dc4", entity_id:"Guru"}}, {name:"Samsara", properties:{file_path:"unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: AyUE-2Uh5Vg (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AyUE-2Uh5Vg)<SEP>YouTube Video: owC8E_G2fY4 (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=owC8E_G2fY4)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Samsara is a concept in Indian philosophy that denotes the cycle of worldly existence and suffering. It is the cycle of rebirth from which humans must awaken to achieve peace, and from which awakening is necessary to attain liberation. The cycle of existence and suffering is characterized by daydreams and worldly attachments. Samsara is also described as a cycle of life and death, influenced by karma and vasanas, and is sometimes referred to as ?bad samsara? in the text. It represents the cycle of life and death that must be transcended for spiritual freedom. In some contexts, Samsara is portrayed as a concept symbolizing worldly existence or suffering, from which Ramya felt liberated in Dasha. Additionally, the concept is mentioned in textual corrections, where it is described as being hidden in a person. Overall, Samsara encapsulates the perpetual cycle of birth, death, and rebirth, driven by karmic forces and attachments, and is the condition from which spiritual awakening or liberation is required.<SEP>Samsara refers to destructive imprints in consciousness caused by unmet emotional needs during infancy.<SEP>Samsara refers to destructive imprints in consciousness caused by unmet emotional needs during infancy.", created_at:1779556303, source_id:"chunk-3269918410ef2996ad74d621f6f6159f<SEP>chunk-a20fa03637522df32905bf3e04315780<SEP>chunk-e0280d57f075227c7dc8487c44357147<SEP>chunk-f736079de24478bec6cb37255e7aac1e<SEP>chunk-498e1fd5e415407ac1ad5829d73bec9b<SEP>chunk-068119dd429404d7b660b1eacf50b8a7<SEP>chunk-05876490ec07e753e9e70eaf93dbcac0<SEP>chunk-5baab383769ea33393f76b07d34a78c0<SEP>chunk-0443cca2d76c87663467e3610969c2ba", entity_id:"Samsara"}}, {name:"Satsang", properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: owC8E_G2fY4 (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=owC8E_G2fY4)", entity_type:"event", truncate:"", description:"Satsang is a spiritual gathering with Sri Krishnaji that influenced the family's business growth.<SEP>Satsang is a spiritual gathering where business growth was discussed.", created_at:1779433874, source_id:"chunk-3a0add62a70895b5ac3db1f7977a8549<SEP>chunk-a8830e719ab8be4a9944bce2ee0a988b", entity_id:"Satsang"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Concept{name: row.name}) SET n += row.properties SET n:base;
