\\\"Anger is an emotional state that can be portrayed as a destructive force, capable of outlasting transient political events and threatening personal relationships. It is also described as a suffering state arising from feeling less important or gifted than others. Anger can lead to negative consequences such as health issues, strained relationships, and self-harm, often through blaming others or oneself. In human behavior, anger is perceived as either a weakness or a catalyst for action, and is analyzed in relation to its suppression and consequences. Additionally, some descriptions note that anger can imprint negative energy on food during cooking. Anger is connected to problems related to itself, implying a cyclical relationship between emotional states and consequences. Finally, anger is an intense emotion that can disrupt relationships and contribute to disconnection.\\\"\
