The relation between Author and Preethaji is characterized by shared spiritual goals centered on engaging with life and pursuing a transformed state through an unconventional perspective that challenges conventional assumptions. They emphasize proactive engagement with life, maintain a lack of disillusionment, and are driven by spiritual passion. Their collaboration includes caring for their parents' health, running the Academy for Consciousness Studies, and parenting their teenage daughter together.", source_id:"chunk-4460c53283867cf0e7a6a331fc3daa9a<SEP>chunk-2b4fda69309d99ad3cadc792e81ed13a<SEP>chunk-bfc9ac02b4b45204e93a15d51a959bb6<SEP>chunk-533c11dca17ed148bc0fe09075977a5a<SEP>chunk-ffbd16a80a3f36425c182278e7bb273d<SEP>chunk-609eba9953b128ee5842ae83faafcdb9<SEP>chunk-8747b8559b6ab050bd73313beb85bb44", entity_id:"Author"}}, {_id:128, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source", entity_type:"organization", truncate:"", description:"An internationally acclaimed academy for consciousness studies that has reached over 69,500 students globally and operates charities and businesses.<SEP>An internationally acclaimed academy founded by Krishnaji and Preethaji, focused on teaching consciousness and transforming lives through education.` - Looks correct.", created_at:1779174767, source_id:"chunk-5e9d081084055b2f138ca25676b72aed<SEP>chunk-23f4ae85323a27ae180ceca7fa33c13a", entity_id:"Consciousness Studies Academy"}}, {_id:129, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"organization", truncate:"", description:"Five global businesses guided by the academy, acting as visionaries and strategic advisors in recent years.", created_at:1779135779, source_id:"chunk-5e9d081084055b2f138ca25676b72aed", entity_id:"Global Business Ventures"}}, {_id:130, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"organization", truncate:"", description:"Two large-scale charities founded by the academy, impacting over 500,000 villagers across more than 1,000 villages.", created_at:1779135779, source_id:"chunk-5e9d081084055b2f138ca25676b72aed", entity_id:"Global Charities Initiative"}}, {_id:131, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Philosophical concept asserting that humans are more than their physical bodies and limited minds, capable of universal harmony.", created_at:1779135779, source_id:"chunk-5e9d081084055b2f138ca25676b72aed", entity_id:"Transcendental Beings"}}, {_id:132, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"person", truncate:"", description:"Villagers in over 1", created_at:1779135779, source_id:"chunk-5e9d081084055b2f138ca25676b72aed", entity_id:"villagers"}}, {_id:133, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"content", truncate:"", description:"An ancient fable used to explain the First Sacred Secret, involving monks and a woman.<SEP>The fable about monks Yesmi and Nomi illustrates the First Sacred Secret through a narrative about compassion and conflict resolution.", created_at:1779136672, source_id:"chunk-cc0f1d606ce37b2df3217415d8473a96<SEP>chunk-7f3bb991411cbbfa162f676b4fd10180<SEP>chunk-3f368851bf5ddb2f8eff6b6b68ee073b", entity_id:"Fable"}}, {_id:134, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source", entity_type:"organization", truncate:"", created_at:1779178792, description:"The monastery is the destination of Yesmi and Nomi after teaching in the village.<SEP>The monastery is the destination for the two monks.<SEP>The monastery is the home of monks Yesmi and Nomi, serving as the narrative setting for the fable.<SEP>The monastery is the destination for the monks after teaching.<SEP>Monastery is a location where the monks are returning, serving as the endpoint of their journey.`<SEP>The monastery is the destination of the monks Yesmi and Nomi, symbolizing a place of spiritual practice and reflection.` - Looks correct.<SEP>The monastery is the destination of the monks, representing a place of spiritual practice and reflection.", source_id:"chunk-cc0f1d606ce37b2df3217415d8473a96<SEP>chunk-2c5321682aea240a40b41c720211188a<SEP>chunk-7f3bb991411cbbfa162f676b4fd10180<SEP>chunk-665f72ba5123be26210ce8f477e2012f<SEP>chunk-50a3afd25409a52a572d62a449dbc4ec<SEP>chunk-23f4ae85323a27ae180ceca7fa33c13a<SEP>chunk-bd28b1a048122e44541304a8505b07db", entity_id:"Monastery"}}, {_id:135, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", created_at:1779183520, description:"Yesmi is a monk in a fable who returns to the monastery and approaches a crying woman in need. He helps her cross the river, demonstrating compassion and practicality, embodying monastic virtues of kindness and service. His actions highlight his role as a compassionate figure who intervenes in the lives of those in distress, showing kindness and service.

Yesmi also represents a \"beautiful state\" in the narrative, characterized by inner simplicity, presence, and a connection to the present moment. This state is free from rumination or anxiety and is associated with positive emotional states and constructive actions. He demonstrates a calm, stress-free condition, harmonious actions without causing stress, and is linked to presence and awareness.

In the story, Yesmi's compassion contrasts with Nomi's preoccupation, emphasizing his focus on the present and the needs of others. He exhibits compassion, releases burdens, and demonstrates connection, problem-solving, and compassionate action without self-centered motives.

Yesmi embodies a beautiful state of consciousness, resolving a woman's problem with compassion and presence. He exhibits calmness, presence, compassion, and inner peace, representing a state of presence and non-suffering. His presence is linked to awareness and he is a character who embodies these qualities.<SEP>Yesmi represents a state of presence and awareness associated with resolving distress and fostering connection.` - Correct. A concept.", source_id:"chunk-cc0f1d606ce37b2df3217415d8473a96<SEP>chunk-2c5321682aea240a40b41c720211188a<SEP>chunk-852cc1672a2a3a688bdf18076d61f76f<SEP>chunk-92e23343f6e8c0c72900c7b35b033bb3<SEP>chunk-7f3bb991411cbbfa162f676b4fd10180<SEP>chunk-184f463e79b52fec37638a498735f009<SEP>chunk-ae33a0629a1035831d09370dbcb6fa05<SEP>chunk-9068ddb93a07ecf743249c1b3afe8709<SEP>chunk-bdc4a608530faeb54a567f51d21bad5a<SEP>chunk-1fc805671f75f5c49fede8b02e05b8db<SEP>chunk-50a3afd25409a52a572d62a449dbc4ec<SEP>chunk-6299fc30fbbfe258eb23a6bd35458a43<SEP>chunk-23f4ae85323a27ae180ceca7fa33c13a<SEP>chunk-bd28b1a048122e44541304a8505b07db<SEP>chunk-1ba7f5be1d21e67ddd5d6d9988215271<SEP>chunk-81f7d5b351616383eb1a7cca9b4d2b48<SEP>chunk-8b68736730809289d016abf18cb33a9d<SEP>chunk-98ebbba09ead01df2486b7e4f58bcc9b", entity_id:"Yesmi"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:`UNIQUE IMPORT LABEL`{`UNIQUE IMPORT ID`: row._id}) SET n += row.properties SET n:base;
