Action is a term associated with reactive behaviors driven by external circumstances, contrasting with intentionality and emotional presence in relationships. It is characterized by a dualistic nature, encompassing \"considered\" and \"inclusive\" aspects, reflecting a paradoxical relationship between intentionality and inclusivity in human behavior. The term also appears in contexts referencing a process to identify and name one's current emotion, though this connection remains implicit.", source_id:"chunk-426c5ab879ce50fae255df16342b8a15<SEP>chunk-70c4972427bbbb91625b1858ddbe811f<SEP>chunk-b0aa1897202602a9be2a7516d39d5400<SEP>chunk-bed30e61f70b382a4a6595c34ba8a934<SEP>chunk-6052761888817e6a639d7d02535dd8c5", entity_id:"Action"}}, {_id:239, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", created_at:1779183668, description:"Desire and reality are unified in the expanded state of consciousness.<SEP>Desire and reality are described as unified within the field of consciousness, emphasizing their interconnectedness in the practice.<SEP>Desire and Reality are treated as one in Soul Sync, reflecting the practice's focus on manifestation.", source_id:"chunk-7e21cbebb168cec17df5a464a689a4f9<SEP>chunk-e69d17b5a95c66d86550266e6f75a794<SEP>chunk-6e3b92943a430e127a61bead1ab61d60", entity_id:"Desire and Reality"}}, {_id:240, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"A count of eight breaths used in specific meditation steps to achieve calm and expansion.", created_at:1779136438, source_id:"chunk-7e21cbebb168cec17df5a464a689a4f9", entity_id:"Eight Breaths"}}] AS row
