UNWIND [{_id:364, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gQiIwfA3mlk)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fdPQxZsPAwI)", entity_type:"creature", truncate:"", created_at:1779217152, description:"The lion whose roar inspires the lion cub, representing authority and power in the forest.<SEP>Lion is mentioned alongside the tiger in the context of influencing animal behavior.<SEP>Lions maintain respectful distance from humans when hungry as part of natural behavior.<SEP>Lion is a wild animal historically associated with physical danger and life-threatening scenarios.<SEP>The lion is another example of a physical danger that historically triggered a stress response for survival.", source_id:"chunk-fe2967cbd738ae1882767972220f2846<SEP>chunk-6dd6f0aed7fea431a27783bb1609b0ed<SEP>chunk-be5b7210ecbddf5ded747efb6c288c98<SEP>chunk-12b99bdaf0b9e3dacedf22c15bf06bc9<SEP>chunk-671c6ddc6c8ba583342b564958bff7bd", entity_id:"Lion"}}, {_id:365, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"creature", truncate:"", description:"A group of sheep that the lion cub grows up with, believing he is one of them.", created_at:1779137399, source_id:"chunk-fe2967cbd738ae1882767972220f2846", entity_id:"Sheep"}}, {_id:366, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hcNDrMy6gCE)<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: nCkbv_lvFfg (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nCkbv_lvFfg)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Rejection, even in small forms during childhood, can cause deep emotional wounds and influence long-term self-perception and social behavior.<SEP>A feeling of inadequacy or dismissal discussed in the video.`<SEP>A suffering state caused by being loved for external attributes rather than intrinsic self.<SEP>Rejection is another emotional state that chokes personal growth without conscious assimilation.", created_at:1779556161, source_id:"chunk-391c88f34f518d5844e754bc2fc76c03<SEP>chunk-938d8c7cf2e140a4e60de3b5d9b45278<SEP>chunk-beeabf4db9d94499feff9e07a340c9a1<SEP>chunk-6d16539213ab1e4cb0268da2ab5977c1", entity_id:"Rejection"}}, {_id:367, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Emotional experiences such as love, care, empathy, connection, joy, rejection, disappointment, and loneliness shape individuals' sense of self and relationships with others.", created_at:1779137426, source_id:"chunk-391c88f34f518d5844e754bc2fc76c03<SEP>chunk-6b077b95a5e468c5e42f57a37944c07d", entity_id:"Emotional Experiences"}}, {_id:368, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Habitual states developed from early emotional experiences affect how individuals feel about themselves and relate to others in adulthood.", created_at:1779137426, source_id:"chunk-391c88f34f518d5844e754bc2fc76c03", entity_id:"Habitual States"}}, {_id:369, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Parental relationships are the first experiences of love, care, empathy, connection, and joy, as well as rejection, disappointment, and loneliness, impacting a child's sense of self and interactions with others.", created_at:1779137426, source_id:"chunk-391c88f34f518d5844e754bc2fc76c03", entity_id:"Parental Relationships"}}, {_id:370, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Early experiences during childhood, including relationships with parents and parental figures, form habitual states that influence self-perception and social interactions.", created_at:1779137426, source_id:"chunk-391c88f34f518d5844e754bc2fc76c03", entity_id:"Early Experiences"}}, {_id:371, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JwMlR98BgrI)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bCzjP2UaKRI)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fj2_d2lNGVk)<SEP>YouTube Video: nen-DB_tz4M (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nen-DB_tz4M)<SEP>YouTube Video: LapJqYf9hzI (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LapJqYf9hzI)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3weAVHuSCxg)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Entity Name: Loneliness

Description List:<SEP>A state of feeling alone, discussed in the context of self-imposed isolation and emotional conflicts.<SEP>Loneliness is an emotional state of isolation, particularly emphasized among youngsters in the context of modern challenges.<SEP>Loneliness is an emotional state of isolation, particularly emphasized among youngsters in the context of modern challenges.<SEP>Increased sense of isolation among young generations, contributing to psychological distress.<SEP>Loneliness is a state of isolation and lack of companionship, frequently experienced after a separation.<SEP>Loneliness is a prolonged state of isolation, disconnected from the active emotion of love.", created_at:1779737968, source_id:"chunk-391c88f34f518d5844e754bc2fc76c03<SEP>chunk-9398fca4f7667d8c5a5db620f32a2795<SEP>chunk-d52f636ec1e248fba87af843ffd93511<SEP>chunk-0abffe0fa33b9e8c05e4d3ce9e08d67e<SEP>chunk-8aad6ef1fd3889e4b8c9933c17173354<SEP>chunk-b0b6f9f02020768407fee531e6074a4d<SEP>chunk-a77f1fee05f090e6b596f48781d6d33a<SEP>chunk-d418467c48468e14dfc470272f04b0d2<SEP>chunk-aaa5c02ef780f417e1e3498aff83c60b<SEP>chunk-5c8f3b58191cd7eb20e97c7adfd8085c<SEP>chunk-5d0f74c4239eabf7a6fea87da28be5d8<SEP>chunk-5506ec1bf2947c78c3b169a20af36482<SEP>chunk-37c881d41553a8a7658ca326a33a2864<SEP>chunk-61a7ee017159ac7e6854fff065426b75<SEP>chunk-959b75d8730e8069b5cdeee7b801f17f<SEP>chunk-0390556d788c91f6a96de617dfba0674<SEP>chunk-965f0460a260b37383e3134a787405f5<SEP>chunk-d720c7b9783846012decda752c188747<SEP>chunk-aec7e5d9768233c70894ac1802b148a7<SEP>chunk-1f205cfd4f752f944e4f589c26e28701<SEP>chunk-baa29517ede049854e2aecf133575342<SEP>chunk-73cf209c2ca0aee45e9dc6e6411c0cb2<SEP>chunk-ad21c8251c43d2428c2c1fc6eaf57acc<SEP>chunk-e8c3861302e4fee45689e6fb65d84e48<SEP>chunk-c2dfb10d73bb85ba3334f2281cc0afee<SEP>chunk-5a1740daf11f031bb2f4e4877b90a316<SEP>chunk-2bfc54003e79d44fa2a7ce956b569e44<SEP>chunk-710110c627104c0a94bd8c9545f51f89<SEP>chunk-86b06c28798f4c4a7bd03b34bd895d71<SEP>chunk-b4ef0432d09dd625d180cc94f3e0ef2e<SEP>chunk-801a54bafa1f63f0a4d091331cafc3d9<SEP>chunk-0bcd34bbf2440bb034ae1a5607edb427", entity_id:"Loneliness"}}, {_id:372, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Emotional wounds resulting from childhood rejections, neglect, or disappointment that influence long-term self-perception and behavior.<SEP>Emotional wounds are deep and lasting impacts from childhood rejections and neglect, forming the ground for the wounded child state.", created_at:1779137449, source_id:"chunk-391c88f34f518d5844e754bc2fc76c03<SEP>chunk-b6d2ea9a34bd43a3b859724cf57d8bec", entity_id:"Emotional Wounds"}}, {_id:373, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"The societal expectation to suppress emotions and prioritize daily duties over emotional well-being, leading to chronic stress and loneliness.", created_at:1779137427, source_id:"chunk-391c88f34f518d5844e754bc2fc76c03", entity_id:"Emotional Compromise"}}, {_id:374, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Government Restrictions refer to lockdown rules and social distancing measures in India.", created_at:1779210956, source_id:"chunk-6239363e43b90d034be5850e9ec19b9d", entity_id:"Government Restrictions"}}, {_id:375, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"UNKNOWN", truncate:"", description:"Neglect in parental relationships leads to emotional wounds that shape habitual behaviors in adulthood.", created_at:1779137427, source_id:"chunk-391c88f34f518d5844e754bc2fc76c03", entity_id:"Neglect"}}, {_id:376, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"person", truncate:"", description:"Salt Seller is a character in the story who sells salt and struggles to sleep due to emotional distress.", created_at:1779137449, source_id:"chunk-b6d2ea9a34bd43a3b859724cf57d8bec", entity_id:"Salt Seller"}}, {_id:377, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Wounded Child State is a psychological condition formed by childhood emotional wounds, unresolved emotional pain, and inner psychological patterns rooted in past hurts and unhealed trauma. It represents an inner psychological pattern characterized by past pain and inner chaos, which can be relived in present life.

The Wounded Child State influences present behavior, self-perception, and relationships, and can affect career and family dynamics, leading to emotional turmoil, self-destructive behaviors, internal conflict, shame, and self-doubt. It is marked by inner chaos and internal conflict, which may manifest as self-destructive behaviors and negatively impact adult behavior, relationships, and self-perception.

The state can emerge from societal conditioning and emotional suppression, marked by shame, self-doubt, and internal conflict stemming from childhood experiences. It may be addressed through interventions such as the Soul Sync Exercise.

In specific cases, such as Andrew's wounded child state, it can cause significant emotional turmoil, negatively impacting career and family dynamics through self-destructive behaviors.<SEP>The wounded child state represents unresolved past traumas and inner conflict that hinder personal growth, characterized by suffering and self-judgment.", created_at:1779183826, source_id:"chunk-b6d2ea9a34bd43a3b859724cf57d8bec<SEP>chunk-749e889c128e710cc18adc38c4d377cb<SEP>chunk-faa97c15f888df1c3373e6c7826983c8<SEP>chunk-f34d4c3475c783164c62af4dbf5b6c3c<SEP>chunk-c9bf814a48dc1240281eb32fd8bfe8b4<SEP>chunk-da4a30723d6bfb88a08e73a51a9a3d62<SEP>chunk-25634a7e16db511e9e5b4a8597da99fd<SEP>chunk-6b077b95a5e468c5e42f57a37944c07d<SEP>chunk-5d0f74c4239eabf7a6fea87da28be5d8<SEP>chunk-0c3de714c4e42df4c68c8fd79dfac5ad", entity_id:"Wounded Child State"}}, {_id:378, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source", entity_type:"person", truncate:"", created_at:1779183742, description:"Flower Seller is a character in the story who sells flowers and hosts the salt seller during the rain.<SEP>A flower seller whose house provided shelter for the fish seller during heavy rain.<SEP>A character in Sri Ramakrishna?s story, representing resilience and adaptability in the face of discomfort.`", source_id:"chunk-b6d2ea9a34bd43a3b859724cf57d8bec<SEP>chunk-d4fb27ed500b1a960390eadd6d011176<SEP>chunk-6b077b95a5e468c5e42f57a37944c07d", entity_id:"Flower Seller"}}, {_id:379, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source", entity_type:"person", truncate:"", description:"Sri Ramakrishna is an Indian mystic who authored a story illustrating the impact of suffering states.<SEP>Sri Ramakrishna is referenced in the book's content for his work on positivity and mindfulness.<SEP>An Indian mystic whose story illustrates the impact of habitual emotional states.<SEP>Sri Ramakrishna is a spiritual figure referenced for his teachings on positivity and mindfulness.", created_at: