UNWIND [{_id:549, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"artifact", truncate:"", description:"The Gift is an item the man uses to convince the woman of his love.", created_at:1779138445, source_id:"chunk-3cea1660026a8c404547b5881940bd50", entity_id:"Gift"}}, {_id:550, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jW3JDLY0cDA)<SEP>YouTube Video: HtmLQkxj8ec (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HtmLQkxj8ec)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Habitual emotional responses such as anxiety, stress, anger, disappointment, jealousy, and indifference, which can escalate without the practice of inner truth.<SEP>Subjective psychological conditions such as connection, excitement, peace, joy, loneliness, hurt, boredom, and indifference.<SEP>Psychological conditions or moods experienced by individuals, such as desperation or hope.<SEP>Emotional states are painful feelings that dissolve as generational hate is addressed.", created_at:1779444174, source_id:"chunk-031bd1294ef04a689b10ae93123dbc7a<SEP>chunk-34273baf53443f0bff0e1b2015dfb920<SEP>chunk-1444d9544f5a6ff9532dfcc5227c350f<SEP>chunk-8b28e95f654546fbfe92679721749ead<SEP>chunk-6a9f2d6a4a0f266522ec5c2fd624dac0", entity_id:"Emotional States"}}, {_id:551, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2DLb6hDIhmg)", entity_type:"UNKNOWN", truncate:"", description:"Nations and communities that underestimated the coronavirus faced severe repercussions.", created_at:1779211082, source_id:"chunk-9428dc8eb300302fda718c2a6b0b9f94", entity_id:"nations, communities"}}, {_id:552, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2DLb6hDIhmg)", entity_type:"UNKNOWN", truncate:"", description:"The coronavirus is metaphorically described as a force of nature, highlighting its uncontrollable and powerful nature.", created_at:1779211082, source_id:"chunk-9428dc8eb300302fda718c2a6b0b9f94", entity_id:"nature's force"}}, {_id:553, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source", entity_type:"person", truncate:"", created_at:1779179248, description:"Diego is a man experiencing severe guilt, depression, and suicidal thoughts after the death of his son, leading to self-imposed suffering and disconnection from his family.<SEP>Diego is a character who experiences guilt over his son's death and seeks forgiveness through meditation and actions.<SEP>A grieving father who struggles with guilt and self-destructive behavior after his son's death.<SEP>Diego is a father who experienced the loss of his son through suicide, leading to his own guilt and depression. He later undergoes a healing process with Krishnaji and plans to hold talent competitions in his son's memory.", source_id:"chunk-aba350ed9d0892b4b1d22f7c1f604b21<SEP>chunk-0c857ef7148c7fabda317a3a8fe52f05<SEP>chunk-214089f71bed8468f80247a24979283e<SEP>chunk-107b2dccdd97eea5e4e04ec3f64a95a9<SEP>chunk-999192b96103e7c498639cfadd062722", entity_id:"Diego"}}, {_id:554, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"event", truncate:"", description:"Meditation with Krishnaji is a session where Diego connects with his son's presence and seeks forgiveness.", created_at:1779138580, source_id:"chunk-0c857ef7148c7fabda317a3a8fe52f05", entity_id:"Meditation with Krishnaji"}}, {_id:555, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"event", truncate:"", description:"Annual Talent Search Competitions are events organized by Diego in his city to honor his son and promote talent.", created_at:1779138580, source_id:"chunk-0c857ef7148c7fabda317a3a8fe52f05", entity_id:"Annual Talent Search Competitions"}}, {_id:556, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"location", truncate:"", created_at:1779142636, description:"City is the location where Diego holds annual talent search competitions, though its specific name is not provided.<SEP>The city where Sunil's daughter resides, where he decides to live part-time to maintain proximity to her.<SEP>A faceless urban environment where the young man feels insignificant and trapped in poverty.", source_id:"chunk-0c857ef7148c7fabda317a3a8fe52f05<SEP>chunk-f8449165361188bfe6afa260ab623922<SEP>chunk-369f0db74a66636fddaa77ce9a54b9b6", entity_id:"City"}}, {_id:557, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"person", truncate:"", description:"His Son is an unnamed character whose death caused Diego's guilt, and who is a source of inspiration for Diego's actions.", created_at:1779138580, source_id:"chunk-0c857ef7148c7fabda317a3a8fe52f05", entity_id:"His Son"}}, {_id:558, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"DJ is a concept related to the son's interests, which influences the type of talent searches Diego organizes.", created_at:1779138580, source_id:"chunk-0c857ef7148c7fabda317a3a8fe52f05", entity_id:"DJ"}}, {_id:559, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"War with Self is a concept representing Diego's internal conflict, which resolves into a sense of calm.", created_at:1779138580, source_id:"chunk-0c857ef7148c7fabda317a3a8fe52f05", entity_id:"War with Self"}}, {_id:560, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"organization", truncate:"", description:"Graduates are individuals who have completed the practice and experienced positive outcomes, including magical resolution of challenges and improved responses to situations.<SEP>Graduates are individuals who have completed the practice and experienced positive outcomes, including magical resolution of situations and improved responses to challenges.", created_at:1779138625, source_id:"chunk-7d095ecda8ad504c7c7ad3c217e955be", entity_id:"Graduates"}}, {_id:561, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"organization", truncate:"", description:"Leaders and seekers are practitioners of The Serene Mind Practice, including leaders, seekers, teenagers, and children, who report positive outcomes from the practice.", created_at:1779138625, source_id:"chunk-7d095ecda8ad504c7c7ad3c217e955be", entity_id:"Leaders and Seekers"}}, {_id:562, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Limited states refer to restrictive mental or emotional conditions that can lead to obsessive behavior, addressed through the practice.", created_at:1779138625, source_id:"chunk-7d095ecda8ad504c7c7ad3c217e955be", entity_id:"Limited States"}}, {_id:563, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"The concept describes situations resolving themselves effortlessly as a result of practicing The Serene Mind Practice.", created_at:1779138625, source_id:"chunk-7d095ecda8ad504c7c7ad3c217e955be", entity_id:"Magical Resolution of Situations"}}, {_id:564, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CZ_r5sYeTyY)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"The Serene Mind Practice is a method to move out of self-obsession into serenity, preventing limited states from becoming obsessive and fostering magical resolution of challenges.<SEP>A five-step practice for achieving clarity and managing emotions through focused observation and breathing exercises.<SEP>The Serene Mind Practice is a three-minute mindfulness method designed to help individuals step out of disturbed states and consciousness, with significant positive impacts on life and the world.<SEP>The Serene Mind Practice is a short but powerful method to help individuals step out of inner disturbance and consciousness disturbances, requiring only three minutes to practice with significant life impact.", created_at:1779248783, source_id:"chunk-7d095ecda8ad504c7c7ad3c217e955be<SEP>chunk-c14547accc3c893d2fdd3408fe344de0<SEP>chunk-c9caee3e34754dd743fb5e0f90ac1a6b<SEP>chunk-132b8aaee32a493c686704b9df170e0b", entity_id:"The Serene Mind Practice"}}, {_id:565, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Refers to enhanced adaptability and imaginative responses to challenges reported by practitioners of The Serene Mind Practice.", created_at:1779138625, source_id:"chunk-7d095ecda8ad504c7c7ad3c217e955be", entity_id:"Improved Challenge Responses"}}, {_id:566, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Fourth step in the Serene Mind Practice involving observing the direction of your thinking to determine if you are obsessing over the past, projecting a chaotic future, or in the present.", created_at:1779138648, source_id:"chunk-c14547accc3c893d2fdd3408fe344de0", entity_id:"STEP FOUR. Observe the direction of thinking"}}, {_id:567, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"First step in the Serene Mind Practice involving sitting still to initiate the practice.", created_at:1779138648, source_id:"chunk-c14547accc3c893d2fdd3408fe344de0", entity_id:"STEP ONE. Sit still"}}, {_id:568, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source", entity_type:"content", truncate:"", description:"An audio guide version of the Serene Mind Practice led by Preethaji, available at www.thefoursacredsecrets.com.<SEP>An audio book edition of the Serene Mind Practice led by Preethaji, available for guided practice.", created_at:1779183930, source_id:"chunk-c14547accc3c893d2fdd3408fe344de0<SEP>chunk-5b0bc29474343c900abfcb530ac6bf39", entity_id:"Audio Book Edition"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:`UNIQUE IMPORT LABEL`{`UNIQUE IMPORT ID`: row._id}) SET n += row.properties SET n:base;
UNWIND [{_id:569, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Third step in the Serene Mind Practice involving observing your emotional state until you discover the exact emotion you are feeling.", created_at:1779138648, source_id:"chunk-c14547accc3c893d2fdd3408fe344de0", entity_id:"STEP THREE. Observe your state"}}, {_id:570, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Second step in the Serene Mind Practice involving deep abdominal breaths with total attention.", created_at:1779138648, source_id:"chunk-c14547accc3c893d2fdd3408fe344de0", entity_id:"STEP TWO. Take three deep abdominal breaths"}}, {_id:571, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Fifth step in the Serene Mind Practice involving imagining a tiny flame at the center of your eyebrows and seeing it move inward to the middle of your skull.", created_at:1779138648, source_id:"chunk-c14547accc3c893d2fdd3408fe344de0", entity_id:"STEP FIVE. Imagine a flame"}}, {_id:572, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source", entity_type:"data", truncate:"", description:"A website where more information about the audio book edition of the Serene Mind Practice can be found.<SEP>A website offering information and access to the audio book edition of the Serene Mind Practice.", created_at:1779183930, source_id:"chunk-c14547accc3c893d2fdd3408fe344de0<SEP>chunk-5b0bc29474343c900abfcb530ac6bf39", entity_id:"www.thefoursacredsecrets.com"}}, {_id:573, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source", entity_type:"content", truncate:"", description:"The Second Sacred Secret is a concept emphasizing understanding and addressing one's inner truth to achieve greatness, as detailed in the source text.<SEP>The Second Sacred Secret is a book by Preethaji that explores the concept of inner truth and its role in achieving greatness.", created_at:1779179249, source_id:"chunk-dfb4cd1f4b16e36588d2ae2b6b987ae7<SEP>chunk-dec047b5cab8e88110c88f8cc2cfcd7d", entity_id:"The Second Sacred Secret"}}, {_id:574, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"method", truncate:"", description:"Three-Minute Pause is a method to reset focus and energy through a brief pause, as described in the text.", created_at:1779138688, source_id:"chunk-dfb4cd1f4b16e36588d2ae2b6b987ae7", entity_id:"Three-Minute Pause"}}, {_id:575, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Nonviolent Resistance is a concept associated with Gandhi's approach to social change through peaceful means.<SEP>Nonviolent resistance is a theme in the source document, advocating for peaceful methods of change.", created_at:1779138711, source_id:"chunk-dfb4cd1f4b16e36588d2ae2b6b987ae7<SEP>chunk-65c5a866de092cd58e4d4a2b1044a21e", entity_id:"Nonviolent Resistance"}}, {_id:577, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=B8wapoLAu84)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", created_at:1779154651, description:"Negative Emotions include anger, shame, stress, and worry, which the text warns against misusing as motivation.<SEP>Negative emotions are discussed as potential sources of dependency and suffering.<SEP>Emotions such as hurt, disappointment, loneliness, anger, and anxiety that dominate when disappointments and longings are unaddressed.<SEP>Negative emotions are caused by habits and can be observed.<SEP>Negative emotions like anger, fear, and sadness are habitual states that impact human behavior and decision-making.<SEP>Negative emotions arise from mental movies about the past and future, and the amygdala is the brain region that feeds on these emotions.<SEP>Emotional states like fear and anxiety, which are triggered by the amygdala.", source_id:"chunk-dfb4cd1f4b16e36588d2ae2b6b987ae7<SEP>chunk-65c5a866de092cd58e4d4a2b1044a21e<SEP>chunk-8aad6ef1fd3889e4b8c9933c17173354<SEP>chunk-6254a0998449b5aae9f36e202e6ddd4f<SEP>chunk-58209224da39691b43cec61c729a13d1<SEP>chunk-f82fe879a5991d902752f3c7f1e83fb7<SEP>chunk-22f4f001e75bdf8bb249d6c2ed547355", entity_id:"Negative Emotions"}}, {_id:578, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Second Life Journey refers to the process of embarking on a new phase of life after understanding one's inner truth, as emphasized in the Second Sacred Secret.<SEP>The second life journey is a transformative phase of life, undertaken with preparedness and self-awareness.", created_at:1779179250, source_id:"chunk-dfb4cd1f4b16e36588d2ae2b6b987ae7<SEP>chunk-14473e52fc6ef3ac056612345f72aa74", entity_id:"Second Life Journey"}}, {_id:579, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=B8wapoLAu84)<SEP>YouTube Video: 6j6EGVpQkI8 (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6j6EGVpQkI8)<SEP>YouTube Video: ajMAwlKh3YM (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ajMAwlKh3YM)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"We need to produce a comprehensive, cohesive summary of the entity \"Present Moment\". The description list includes many points. We need to synthesize into multiple paragraphs, plain text, objective third-person, mention the full name at the beginning, within 600 tokens.

We have to consider conflicts: The description list includes many points, but they are consistent. So we just need to integrate.

We need to ensure we cover:

- Definition: living in the current moment with awareness and acceptance, central to achieving a Serene Mind.
- Being in the present moment is possible and helps in solving problems.
- Being in the present moment allows for balance, practicality, and solving problems by shifting activity from the amygdala to the prefrontal cortex.
- The state of being aware of the current time, linked to solving problems.
- Being preoccupied with oneself and one's thoughts imprisons a person in loneliness.
- The present moment represents a state of awareness in enlightenment, free from fixation on past or future.
- The present moment is the focus in enlightenment, where one lives fully in the now without being pushed toward the past or future.

We need to structure into paragraphs:

Paragraph 1: Definition and core concept (Serene Mind, awareness, acceptance).

Paragraph 2: Benefits and mechanisms (problem solving, balance, amygdala to prefrontal cortex).

