 shaped by societal pressures, leading to behaviors like judgment and distancing from others.", created_at:1779139498, source_id:"chunk-c5db2181b0244c95f353d5c0b1c153ef<SEP>chunk-53499f381af4c99f9a37a7d03455b285", entity_id:"Self-Preoccupied Individuals"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:`UNIQUE IMPORT LABEL`{`UNIQUE IMPORT ID`: row._id}) SET n += row.properties SET n:base;
UNWIND [{_id:610, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UrVvSqKYU8c)<SEP>YouTube Video: ajMAwlKh3YM (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ajMAwlKh3YM)<SEP>YouTube Video: BZDXIQwOPdU (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BZDXIQwOPdU)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1kS_mQaBLdg)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Self is understood as the individual's internal relationship with themselves, encompassing both moments of care and dissatisfaction. It also represents an individual's consciousness and identity, described as a playground for intelligence and creativity. In this sense, the self is established in itself, characterized by self-awareness and alignment with one's senses, breath, and inner divine.

During Kundalini awakening, the self is experienced as the true nature of existence, embodying universal oneness and interconnectedness with the universe. The sense of self can expand or be absent in certain states of consciousness, reflecting its fluid nature.

Self-perception and identity are further shaped by societal beauty norms and personal growth, influencing how the self is understood and expressed. These aspects collectively define the self as a multifaceted construct that integrates personal awareness, creative potential, and relational dynamics.<SEP>Self is defined by ideals and is central to moral judgment.<SEP>Self is the individual's own consciousness and sense of being, which expands and transforms.<SEP>Self is the individual's own consciousness and sense of being, which expands and transforms.<SEP>The concept of \"self\" relates to the individual's sense of identity and awareness expanding to include others.<SEP>The concept of \"self\" relates to the individual's sense of identity and awareness expanding to include others.", created_at:1779669102, source_id:"chunk-2e1251c183d277453a1b96fbfae7185f<SEP>chunk-a5ed3c3b69f89f61229321dd09c0168c<SEP>chunk-160859532101196271f783ac5fd9a047<SEP>chunk-6ceaf029b184877ef7237e73de7e90eb<SEP>chunk-b04f7ebc196bc2024dc00fdd71633076<SEP>chunk-d3b0ed6747a54a9af9e558b6935aa651<SEP>chunk-9687f9221e8ea7d2650809521e33cd96<SEP>chunk-a6affe7a665bbb46d2be844611d794d1<SEP>chunk-c088c9de5db4ddb6d01a048401214aef<SEP>chunk-607beefb79fd1c2b867abf7979a1dbfc", entity_id:"Self"}}, {_id:611, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Moments when the individual experiences care, respect, or acceptance toward themselves.", created_at:1779138817, source_id:"chunk-2e1251c183d277453a1b96fbfae7185f", entity_id:"Moments of Self-Care"}}, {_id:612, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8mmungGgDNw)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", created_at:1779224834, description:"<think>
Okay, let's tackle this. The user wants me to extract the actual spiritual teaching or concept definition from the contaminated text provided. The contaminated text includes a lot of developer instructions and meta-descriptions mixed with the real content.

First, I need to identify the real spiritual content. The entity in question is \"Inner War.\" Looking through the text, there are several mentions of what Inner War refers to. The first part talks about internal conflict and unhappiness driving individuals toward addictive behaviors. Then there's another description mentioning a state of internal conflict between one's authentic self and societal expectations leading to unhappiness. However, the text also notes that these descriptions are part of the same concept, with variations like self-obsession, self-criticism, etc.

The key here is to merge these descriptions into a coherent definition. The main points are internal conflict, unhappiness, addictive behaviors, and the clash between authentic self and societal expectations. The developer instructions and formatting details (like JSON structures and merging processes) need to be stripped out. The final answer should be a clean, concise description without any extra information. Since the text confirms that all descriptions refer to the same concept, I can combine them into a single summary focusing on the core elements: internal conflict, self-related negative emotions, and the drive towards addictive behaviors as an escape.
</think>

Inner War refers to a state of internal conflict and unhappiness that drives individuals toward addictive behaviors as an escape. It involves psychological struggles such as self-obsession, self-criticism, dissatisfaction, and chaos, often arising from unresolved tensions between one's authentic self and external pressures or societal expectations.", source_id:"chunk-2e1251c183d277453a1b96fbfae7185f<SEP>chunk-6ad010179b68a77812793b24f711cf95<SEP>chunk-c756fff1f643175625bc8f48eb702151<SEP>chunk-dc33576be7c40b3be079f258d63f03be<SEP>chunk-676c070f41c08ddde395290878529cf3<SEP>chunk-1a4e20db18753630cc0835f806d71f29<SEP>chunk-6d0566c8fa6f2aed45fb2e69b00761b1<SEP>chunk-5c02e046d7832f0655166e3f716f3e10<SEP>chunk-246826c01e25761bf87cb37c0f82bbb8<SEP>chunk-66f6c16a0cd4b4ef4b399e98335000b4<SEP>chunk-954c4e66e25d390d543a0361e6284f30", entity_id:"Inner War"}}, {_id:613, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Moments when the individual feels dissatisfaction, dislike, or discomfort with themselves.", created_at:1779138817, source_id:"chunk-2e1251c183d277453a1b96fbfae7185f", entity_id:"Moments of Self-Dissatisfaction"}}, {_id:614, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"External solutions and escapes sought during moments of self-dissatisfaction.", created_at:1779138817, source_id:"chunk-2e1251c183d277453a1b96fbfae7185f", entity_id:"External Solutions and Escapes"}}, {_id:615, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"External solutions refer to behaviors like substance use or other escapes to address emotional distress.<SEP>External solutions are criticized as ineffective for addressing the root cause of unhappiness, which stems from internal misalignment.<SEP>Seeking solutions outside oneself to address internal conflicts, highlighted as a common but insufficient approach.<SEP>Seeking solutions outside oneself (e.g., substances, relationships) to address internal issues.", created_at:1779184195, source_id:"chunk-0e910622cdbaf731d9c63e3af759ab25<SEP>chunk-53499f381af4c99f9a37a7d03455b285<SEP>chunk-e22f7c2305a6d6df213efae54a651699<SEP>chunk-66f6c16a0cd4b4ef4b399e98335000b4", entity_id:"External Solutions"}}, {_id:616, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source", entity_type:"naturalobject", truncate:"", description:"Narcotics are substances used by individuals to escape internal conflict, often leading to harmful consequences.<SEP>Substances used as a coping mechanism for internal turmoil.", created_at:1779184193, source_id:"chunk-0e910622cdbaf731d9c63e3af759ab25<SEP>chunk-035b6c44730bb7cdf05bfef04ef27b03", entity_id:"Narcotics"}}, {_id:617, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source", entity_type:"naturalobject", truncate:"", description:"Alcohol is a substance consumed by many to cope with self-doubt and emotional turmoil.<SEP>Substance used to escape self-related distress.", created_at:1779184193, source_id:"chunk-0e910622cdbaf731d9c63e3af759ab25<SEP>chunk-035b6c44730bb7cdf05bfef04ef27b03", entity_id:"Alcohol"}}, {_id:618, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Suicide represents an extreme outcome of unresolved internal conflict and self-doubt.<SEP>A drastic outcome linked to unresolved internal conflict.", created_at:1779184193, source_id:"chunk-0e910622cdbaf731d9c63e3af759ab25<SEP>chunk-035b6c44730bb7cdf05bfef04ef27b03", entity_id:"Suicide"}}, {_id:619, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", created_at:1779184195, description:"Self-doubt refers to a psychological state where individuals question their self-worth and capabilities, leading to negative behaviors and mental health issues.<SEP>Self-doubt is a psychological state characterized by a lack of confidence in one's abilities or decisions.<SEP>Lack of confidence in oneself, stemming from self-criticism or societal pressures.", source_id:"chunk-0e910622cdbaf731d9c63e3af759ab25<SEP>chunk-2cc93fe7ed8db16f45e89fcd38b3ac24<SEP>chunk-66f6c16a0cd4b4ef4b399e98335000b4", entity_id:"Self-Doubt"}}, {_id:620, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"The internal divide describes the psychological conflict between self-acceptance and self-doubt.<SEP>An ever-widening internal conflict leading to self-destructive behaviors and indecision.", created_at:1779184193, source_id:"chunk-0e910622cdbaf731d9c63e3af759ab25<SEP>chunk-035b6c44730bb7cdf05bfef04ef27b03", entity_id:"Internal Divide"}}, {_id:621, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Important decisions of our lives, such as career, relationships, and business partnerships, are often approached indecisively due to internal conflict.", created_at:1779138887, source_id:"chunk-3a9f26816f36d2d6507e237b6a559579", entity_id:"Important Decisions of Our Lives"}}, {_id:622, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2DLb6hDIhmg)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VTx4G0KEuUE)", entity_type:"creature", truncate:"", description:"Elephant in heat is described as acting erratically, symbolizing the challenge to philosophical ideals in practical situations.<SEP>Elephants are large land mammals referenced in the context of human exploitation and conservation discussions.", created_at:1779670567, source_id:"chunk-2ed6c538824d03e53845129e9fe68f60<SEP>chunk-fbc362953fe784a8510b72471b749390", entity_id:"Elephant"}}, {_id:623, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Eeny Meeny Miney Mo is a children's game method symbolizing reliance on luck over deliberate decision-making in important life choices.<SEP>A childhood game used in the text as a metaphor for indecisive decision-making.", created_at:1779184018, source_id:"chunk-3a9f26816f36d2d6507e237b6a559579<SEP>chunk-2cc93fe7ed8db16f45e89fcd38b3ac24", entity_id:"Eeny Meeny Miney Mo"}}, {_id:624, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"event", truncate:"", description:"The Game of Tag is used as a metaphor to illustrate indecisive decision-making, where random selection replaces clear choices.", created_at:1779138887, source_id:"chunk-3a9f26816f36d2d6507e237b6a559579", entity_id:"Game of Tag"}}, {_id:625, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"person", truncate:"", description:"mit suicide is referenced in the context of discussing internal conflict and self-war, highlighting the consequences of being at war with oneself.", created_at:1779138887, source_id:"chunk-3a9f26816f36d2d6507e237b6a559579", entity_id:"mit suicide"}}, {_id:626, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0k5f8G9uXqY)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"happiness is mentioned as unattainable when at war with oneself, emphasizing the need for internal peace.<SEP>A universal human emotion associated with positive emotions, varying in expression.", created_at:1779157775, source_id:"chunk-3a9f26816f36d2d6507e237b6a559579<SEP>chunk-264fb8cd6c5c93babb84a7f63f71ecc5", entity_id:"happiness"}}, {_id:627, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oUCZWSi8zY4)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", created_at:1779152718, description:"wealth is listed as one of the areas impacted by being at war with oneself.<SEP>Wealth is discussed in the context of its instability when the spirit of inclusivity is not embodied.<SEP>wealth is a concept mentioned in the text, determined to be correctly used without homophones.", source_id:"chunk-3a9f26816f36d2d6507e237b6a559579<SEP>chunk-7f96797acd949b60d31248b83d9abf45<SEP>chunk-b9f36968ebf7bca3d8efa72e74d0fd0d", entity_id:"wealth"}}, {_id:628, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"relationships are among the aspects affected by internal conflict, mentioned alongside wealth, leisure, and success.<SEP>Relationships refer to the connections between individuals, which can be transformed through spiritual vision to foster joy and fulfillment.", created_at:1779141102, source_id:"chunk-3a9f26816f36d2d6507e237b6a559579<SEP>chunk-25a61dd1a643342f5252980f3c78e37e<SEP>chunk-56d49489b1f42f899d9566a254886c2c", entity_id:"relationships"}}, {_id:631, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"The ten heads symbolize Ravana's internal conflict, representing his dissenting values and obsessive desires.", created_at:1779138908, source_id:"chunk-e8cb0cf14adb586ae1629961d6d5940a", entity_id:"Ten Heads"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:`UNIQUE IMPORT LABEL`{`UNIQUE IMPORT ID`: row._id}) SET n += row.properties SET n:base;
UNWIND [{_id:632, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: 1_-cZz8YRFw (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1_-cZz8YRFw)", entity_type:"event", truncate:"", description:"The Ramayana is an ancient Indian epic poem depicting the conflict between Rama and Ravana, with Ravana's actions leading to his downfall.<SEP>The Ramayana is an ancient Indian epic used as an example to illustrate the consequences of internal conflict.<SEP>The Ramayana is a classical Indian epic featuring the story of Ahalya's transformation and redemption.<SEP>The Ramayana is a classical Indian epic featuring the story of Ahalya's transformation and redemption.<SEP>The Ramayana is an ancient Indian epic that includes the story of Ahalya.", created_at:1779564399, source_id:"chunk-e8cb0cf14adb586ae1629961d6d5940a<SEP>chunk-afc14563513f7a4dcf36c1ff3fddd517<SEP>chunk-ea1f0fc5a4bd6b550f008cf8e4905da5<SEP>chunk-f35ecb38bfeca95ba27fabf08e8561a8", entity_id:"Ramayana"}}, {_id:633, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: mmpmX3-qfc4 (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mmpmX3-qfc4)<SEP>YouTube Video: 1_-cZz8YRFw (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1_-cZz8YRFw)", entity_type:"location", truncate:"", description:"Ravana's kingdom, which faced destruction due to his actions and the consequences of the Ramayana's narrative.<SEP>The Kingdom is the setting where the King rules and where the search for a happy man takes place.<SEP>The Kingdom is the setting of the story and the domain of the King.<SEP>The Kingdom is the setting where the King rules and where the search for a happy man takes place.<SEP>The kingdom is a location that was divided and given to Duryodhana's cousins, causing conflict and", created_at:1779564579, source_id:"chunk-e8cb0cf14adb586ae1629961d6d5940a<SEP>chunk-f72de7c8d762c18a6655f15c49149836<SEP>chunk-2906abe5180c989f9b833008109705f4<SEP>chunk-cdfac554a3f7f2ebcb638a60cb844514", entity_id:"Kingdom"}}, {_id:634, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source", entity_type:"person", truncate:"", created_at:1779184018, description:"Ravana is a complex character from the Ramayana, portrayed as a scholar-king with internal conflicts and destructive tendencies despite his virtues.<SEP>Ravana is a mythological figure depicted as a man with ten heads, symbolizing his inner conflict and self-destructive tendencies due to dissenting values and obsessive desires.<SEP>Ravana is a figure who succumbed to conflicting desires despite knowing their destructive consequences, leading to his downfall and the collapse of his kingdom.<SEP>Ravana, the ten-headed king, symbolizes internal conflict between desires and moral dilemmas in the context of action.<SEP>Ravana is a historical figure from the Ramayana, depicted as a conflicted king whose inner war between dissenting values led to self-destruction and destruction of his kingdom.<SEP>Ravana is a figure from mythology who struggled with inner conflict and desires, leading to his downfall and the impact on his kingdom.`<SEP>Ravana is a historical figure from the Ramayana, depicted as a conflicted king whose inner turmoil led to self-destruction and downfall.", source_id:"chunk-e8cb0cf14adb586ae1629961d6d5940a<SEP>chunk-6ad010179b68a77812793b24f711cf95<SEP>chunk-c3c756183e3f4bbcd6f10defea6c686f<SEP>chunk-cde14d696f27021b8bd46431e4e80d28<SEP>chunk-676c070f41c08ddde395290878529cf3<SEP>chunk-747dd6f3fc344d596e672f021c5892ee<SEP>chunk-cb8bc4106969c883bf9c7f5bf8e466fc", entity_id:"Ravana"}}, {_id:635, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Conceptual forces driving Ravana's self-trapped state, manifesting as conflicting ideologies and ambitions.", created_at:1779138908, source_id:"chunk-e8cb0cf14adb586ae1629961d6d5940a", entity_id:"Dissenting Values and Obsessive Desires"}}, {_id:636, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"person", truncate:"", description:"The hero of the Ramayana, whose actions and ideals contrast with Ravana's, leading to the kingdom's fate.", created_at:1779138908, source_id:"chunk-e8cb0cf14adb586ae1629961d6d5940a", entity_id:"Rama"}}, {_id:637, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"This philosophical question explores the paradox of moral decline in individuals or groups, linked to inner conflict and conflicting values.", created_at:1779138928, source_id:"chunk-6ad010179b68a77812793b24f711cf95", entity_id:"Why Do Good People Become Bad?"}}, {_id:638, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Self-destructive behavior arises from unresolved inner conflict, manifesting as actions that harm the individual and those around them.", created_at:1779138928, source_id:"chunk-6ad010179b68a77812793b24f711cf95", entity_id:"Self-Destructive Behavior"}}, {_id:639, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Conflicting desires are opposing motivations (e.g., career vs. family, ambition vs. ethics) that create internal turmoil and hinder decision-making.", created_at:1779138928, source_id:"chunk-6ad010179b68a77812793b24f711cf95", entity_id:"Conflicting Desires"}}, {_id:640, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: odNtpKqbCQo (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=odNtpKqbCQo)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", created_at:1779448004, description:"Dissatisfaction arises from unmet desires and unresolved inner conflict, potentially escalating into depression or self-hatred.<SEP>Dissatisfaction is a state leading to destructive outcomes like addictions.<SEP>Dissatisfaction is mentioned as a state linked to destruction in the context.", source_id:"chunk-c3c756183e3f4bbcd6f10defea6c686f<SEP>chunk-30142fb409cd6113794311c0e52cc0fc<SEP>chunk-67c71335838e7d9c72ee9c00d04337d4", entity_id:"Dissatisfaction"}}, {_id:641, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Battleground metaphorically represents the inner world where conflicting desires, virtues, and vices clash, creating emotional turmoil.", created_at:1779138946, source_id:"chunk-c3c756183e3f4bbcd6f10defea6c686f", entity_id:"Battleground"}}, {_id:642, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", created_at:1779184030, description:"The Shrinking Self is a psychological construct that can be interpreted in two primary ways. One interpretation describes it as a state in which the limited sense of self dissolves, leading to a condition of undivided consciousness and a cessation of comparison with others. The other interpretation characterizes it as a maladaptive psychological state marked by persistent self-doubt, the need to compare oneself with others, and resulting feelings of inferiority, low self-esteem, and insignificance. These perspectives reflect both a transformative potential and a chronic, negative pattern of self-evaluation.

In the maladaptive view, the shrinking self is fueled by self-comparison, which drives self-consciousness, insecurity, and a feeling of being insignificant. It often leads individuals to derive self-worth from external validation, resulting in chronic dissatisfaction and a perception of life as an endless race. The state may also manifest as avoidance of life?s joys, as individuals become preoccupied with measuring themselves against others. Some descriptions further note that this condition can cause self-consciousness, comparison, and feelings of insignificance, and may be exemplified by specific behavior patterns, such as those observed in a person named Alex.

The concept is also linked to the notion of self-doubt and the need to compare oneself with others, which can produce feelings of inferiority. In some accounts, the shrinking self is described as a state where individuals derive self-worth from external validation and comparisons, leading to chronic dissatisfaction. Conversely, other descriptions emphasize the dissolution of a limited sense of self, resulting in undivided consciousness and a cessation of comparison.

Because the term is used across these varied contexts, it encompasses both a potentially beneficial transformation of self-perception and a persistent, negative pattern of self-evaluation. The descriptions vary in emphasis, with some focusing on the psychological mechanisms of comparison and low self-esteem, while others highlight the dissolution of the limited self and the cessation of comparison. The term remains a useful label for discussing the complex interplay between self-perception, social comparison, and emotional well-being.", source_id:"chunk-670e795b68d71dbf734feac6e97cfa1f<SEP>chunk-063a5196900a330ccb49599d4025a638<SEP>chunk-13c1b39086ccfd163efe6f6f872777c0<SEP>chunk-0b07ef4dcf56fe79aaec78af52489ef5<SEP>chunk-da4b247a4eac03fe686b0059bd126928<SEP>chunk-676c070f41c08ddde395290878529cf3<SEP>chunk-747dd6f3fc344d596e672f021c5892ee<SEP>chunk-837d0412addc5b4967790622264e22cc<SEP>chunk-cb8bc4106969c883bf9c7f5bf8e466fc", entity_id:"Shrinking Self"}}, {_id:643, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"The \"Warring Self\" refers to internal conflicts that manifest as destructive forces when individuals embrace expressions of self-sabotage or negative self-perception.<SEP>Warring Self represents a state of internal conflict and self-criticism, as described in the Soul Sync Exercise.<SEP>The Warring Self represents a state of internal conflict and discord with oneself and the world.<SEP>Warring Self represents a state of internal conflict and self-criticism, characterized by struggle with oneself and external factors.", created_at:1779179356, source_id:"chunk-670e795b68d71dbf734feac6e97cfa1f<SEP>chunk-f184ea56bcea598aa525718d96f6e142<SEP>chunk-afc14563513f7a4dcf36c1ff3fddd517<SEP>chunk-6af7eefe80697b9b2cf1b0520fd6a984", entity_id:"Warring Self"}}, {_id:644, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"event", truncate:"", description:"Mystic meditation with Krishnaji is an event where Alex experiences a dissolution of self and transformation in consciousness.", created_at:1779138979, source_id:"chunk-063a5196900a330ccb49599d4025a638", entity_id:"Mystic Meditation with Krishnaji"}}, {_id:645, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Inner disharmony refers to Alex's persistent state of self-criticism and comparison that dissolved during his transformation.", created_at:1779138979, source_id:"chunk-063a5196900a330ccb49599d4025a638", entity_id:"Inner Disharmony"}}, {_id:646, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Destructive Self is a psychological concept representing a manifestation of inner conflict that can lead to harmful behaviors such as aggression or hatred. It is characterized by emotional imbalance, impulsivity, and a need to dominate others, often resulting in self-destructive behavior. In some accounts, the destructive self contributes to an inner war, driving the need to dominate others, and can manifest as aggression and conflict, exemplified by Greg's post-divorce actions.

The destructive self is also described as a psychological state where individuals attempt to transcend through renouncing behavior, culture, or language, though this perspective is less common. It is further defined as a self-destructive mindset that perpetuates inner division, and as an inner state driven by comparisons between reality and idealized scenarios, manifesting as emotional imbalance, aggression, and unhealthy relationships. Some descriptions note that it can manifest as perfectionism, ruthlessness, or addiction to power, all of which are underpinned by emotional imbalance and impulsivity.

Collectively, these descriptions portray the destructive self as a multifaceted psychological condition that fuels inner conflict, self-destructive tendencies, and harmful behaviors, while also highlighting its role in perpetuating inner war and the need to dominate others. The concept underscores the complexity of inner division and the various ways it can manifest, from aggression and conflict to perfectionism and addiction to power.", created_at:1779184143, source_id:"chunk-13c1b39086ccfd163efe6f6f872777c0<SEP>chunk-a2bc52698450e6bd9eed995a65131be2<SEP>chunk-3c5cad218c7d45700a257c9263d28c19<SEP>chunk-0b07ef4dcf56fe79aaec78af52489ef5<SEP>chunk-48d38d40b501a5ac9741fdde5e643c26<SEP>chunk-747dd6f3fc344d596e672f021c5892ee<SEP>chunk-837d0412addc5b4967790622264e22cc<SEP>chunk-813e5d6774fbe0673f530d4b67ec6629", entity_id:"Destructive Self"}}, {_id:647, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source", entity_type:"person", truncate:"", description:"Alicia is a person involved in a long-term relationship with Greg and facing marital challenges.<SEP>Alicia is Greg's ex-wife, whom he blames for his unhappiness and seeks to make her life difficult post-divorce.<SEP>Alicia is a person in a troubled marriage with Greg, later divorcing after their daughter leaves home.<SEP>Alicia is a person involved in a destructive relationship with Greg post-divorce, marked by blame and emotional imbalance.`<SEP>Alicia is a character in a troubled marriage with Greg, described as loud and dominant during their relationship.<SEP>Alicia is Greg's ex-wife, described as loud and dominant during their marriage, later blamed by Greg for his unhappiness.", created_at:1779184127, source_id:"chunk-13c1b39086ccfd163efe6f6f872777c0<SEP>chunk-a2bc52698450e6bd9eed995a65131be2<SEP>chunk-da4b247a4eac03fe686b0059bd126928<SEP>chunk-747dd6f3fc344d596e672f021c5892ee<SEP>chunk-837d0412addc5b4967790622264e22cc<SEP>chunk-813e5d6774fbe0673f530d4b67ec6629", entity_id:"Alicia"}}, {_id:648, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source", entity_type:"person", truncate:"", description:"Greg is a person who undergoes a transformation post-divorce, exhibiting destructive behavior driven by hatred.<SEP>Greg is a man who becomes obsessed with revenge after his divorce, manifesting traits of the destructive self such as emotional imbalance and impulsivity.<SEP>Greg is a financially independent individual who develops a destructive self after divorcing Alicia, driven by resentment and comparison.<SEP>Greg is a person who manifested a destructive self post-divorce, characterized by hatred, aggression, and obsession with retribution.`<SEP>Greg is a character who transitions from submissiveness to aggression post-divorce, driven by pent-up anger.<SEP>Greg is a man who becomes obsessed with retaliating against his ex-wife Alicia after their divorce, driven by pent-up anger and a sense of betrayal.", created_at:1779184127, source_id:"chunk-13c1b39086ccfd163efe6f6f872777c0<SEP>chunk-a2bc52698450e6bd9eed995a65131be2<SEP>chunk-da4b247a4eac03fe686b0059bd126928<SEP>chunk-747dd6f3fc344d596e672f021c5892ee<SEP>chunk-837d0412addc5b4967790622264e22cc<SEP>chunk-813e5d6774fbe0673f530d4b67ec6629", entity_id:"Greg"}}, {_id:649, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source", entity_type:"location", truncate:"", description:"Switzerland is the country of origin for the couple Alicia and Greg.<SEP>Switzerland is the home country of Alicia and Greg, contextualizing their marital struggles.", created_at:1779184017, source_id:"chunk-13c1b39086ccfd163efe6f6f872777c0<SEP>chunk-837d0412addc5b4967790622264e22cc", entity_id:"Switzerland"}}, {_id:650, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"UNKNOWN", truncate:"", description:"Alicia and Greg are a couple from Switzerland facing marital issues.", created_at:1779139015, source_id:"chunk-13c1b39086ccfd163efe6f6f872777c0", entity_id:"Alicia and Greg"}}, {_id:651, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"UNKNOWN", truncate:"", description:"The shrinking self is fueled by comparing oneself to others and perceiving inadequacy.", created_at:1779139015, source_id:"chunk-13c1b39086ccfd163efe6f6f872777c0", entity_id:"comparison to others"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:`UNIQUE IMPORT LABEL`{`UNIQUE IMPORT ID`: row._id}) SET n += row.properties SET n:base;
UNWIND [{_id:652, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"UNKNOWN", truncate:"", description:"The shrinking self leads to self-consciousness and avoidance of life's joys.", created_at:1779139016, source_id:"chunk-13c1b39086ccfd163efe6f6f872777c0", entity_id:"self-consciousness"}}, {_id:653, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: ZD1nQPtpojM (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZD1nQPtpojM)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", created_at:1779408825, description:"The divorce between Greg and Alicia triggers significant changes in Greg's behavior, including the manifestation of the destructive self.<SEP>Divorce is mentioned as a potential outcome of a successful marriage.<SEP>The divorce of Alicia and Greg occurs after their daughter leaves for college, driven by unresolved marital issues.<SEP>Divorce is the legal dissolution of a marriage.", source_id:"chunk-a2bc52698450e6bd9eed995a65131be2<SEP>chunk-d97614999399e6f5f1181bdaebd85f12<SEP>chunk-ecacbf92f0c8b457e3e7365b88b0c5b9<SEP>chunk-837d0412addc5b4967790622264e22cc<SEP>chunk-f5f14fddf14672b2d29a6d11525514fd", entity_id:"Divorce"}}, {_id:654, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Pent-up anger and aggression are emotions that Greg harbors and acts upon after his divorce, driving his actions against Alicia.", created_at:1779139042, source_id:"chunk-a2bc52698450e6bd9eed995a65131be2", entity_id:"Pent-up Anger and Aggression"}}, {_id:655, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"The Inert Self is a concept characterized by indifference, lack of responsibility, laziness, procrastination, lack of drive, and lack of motivation.<SEP>The inert self represents a state of passivity, laziness, and lack of motivation characterized by procrastination and daydreaming.", created_at:1779179501, source_id:"chunk-3c5cad218c7d45700a257c9263d28c19<SEP>chunk-2a44f8cb9c9f8ea13650035b5bbd408c", entity_id:"The Inert Self"}}, {_id:656, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Learning Disability is a concept that prevents Beth from achieving the same success as her siblings and affects her self-perception.", created_at:1779139066, source_id:"chunk-3c5cad218c7d45700a257c9263d28c19", entity_id:"Learning Disability"}}, {_id:657, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: odNtpKqbCQo (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=odNtpKqbCQo)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Vicious Cycle is a concept where Beth overeats, does not exercise or work, loses confidence, and makes foolish investments.<SEP>Vicious cycle denotes a self-perpetuating pattern where addictions prevent finding meaning or purpose in life.<SEP>Vicious cycle refers to the destructive loop of addictions preventing meaning and purpose.<SEP>Vicious cycle describes the self-perpetuating nature of addictions that consume individuals.<SEP>Vicious Cycle describes a self-perpetuating pattern where addictions lead to further physical and emotional consumption, eroding personal agency.", created_at:1779447614, source_id:"chunk-3c5cad218c7d45700a257c9263d28c19<SEP>chunk-30142fb409cd6113794311c0e52cc0fc<SEP>chunk-fd0cf329c3a40648553339d60f0ac0b7<SEP>chunk-e53aa20908f0e3dc300b2226e52897f3<SEP>chunk-e27c90d3f030c932363441c1ed78bf62<SEP>chunk-fafff025e01a29bbcee9969fc4559382", entity_id:"Vicious Cycle"}}, {_id:658, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"The Competitive Self is a concept that contributes to the inner war, driving the need to dominate others.", created_at:1779139066, source_id:"chunk-3c5cad218c7d45700a257c9263d28c19", entity_id:"Competitive Self"}}, {_id:659, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source", entity_type:"person", truncate:"", description:"Beth is a person who experiences a learning disability, parental taunts, and engages in a vicious cycle of unhealthy behaviors.<SEP>Beth is a person trapped in an inert self due to lifelong comparisons with her siblings, leading to self-destructive behaviors.<SEP>Beth is a person who struggled with self-comparison, parental criticism, and a vicious cycle of negative behaviors leading to self-destructive patterns.<SEP>Beth is a person who experienced an inert self due to lifelong comparisons with her siblings, leading to feelings of inadequacy.`<SEP>Beth struggles with self-comparison to her siblings, leading to a cycle of self-destructive behavior including overeating and poor financial decisions.", created_at:1779184127, source_id:"chunk-3c5cad218c7d45700a257c9263d28c19<SEP>chunk-da4b247a4eac03fe686b0059bd126928<SEP>chunk-2a44f8cb9c9f8ea13650035b5bbd408c<SEP>chunk-747dd6f3fc344d596e672f021c5892ee<SEP>chunk-813e5d6774fbe0673f530d4b67ec6629", entity_id:"Beth"}}, {_id:660, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Life as a War is a concept where the Inert Self, Competitive Self, and Destructive Self are in conflict.", created_at:1779139066, source_id:"chunk-3c5cad218c7d45700a257c9263d28c19", entity_id:"Life as a War"}}, {_id:661, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Unhealthy Relationships are a result of the inner war, where the Inert Self makes enemies of friends and family.<SEP>Unhealthy relationships refer to dysfunctional interactions that contribute to inner conflict and self-destructive behaviors.", created_at:1779179501, source_id:"chunk-3c5cad218c7d45700a257c9263d28c19<SEP>chunk-2a44f8cb9c9f8ea13650035b5bbd408c", entity_id:"Unhealthy Relationships"}}, {_id:662, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", created_at:1779184128, description:"A psychological state characterized by indifference, lack of responsibility, laziness, and procrastination, leading to giving up and lack of motivation.<SEP>The inert self refers to a state of passivity and resignation resulting from chronic self-comparison and perceived inadequacy.`<SEP>The inert self is marked by indifference, procrastination, and lack of motivation, often resulting in daydreaming and unhealthy relationships.", source_id:"chunk-0b07ef4dcf56fe79aaec78af52489ef5<SEP>chunk-747dd6f3fc344d596e672f021c5892ee<SEP>chunk-813e5d6774fbe0673f530d4b67ec6629", entity_id:"Inert Self"}}, {_id:663, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"method", truncate:"", description:"Engaging in high-risk activities as an attempt to boost self-esteem and project a glorious self-image.", created_at:1779139092, source_id:"chunk-0b07ef4dcf56fe79aaec78af52489ef5", entity_id:"Adventure Sports"}}, {_id:664, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"UNKNOWN", truncate:"", description:"The inert self leads to giving up hope that positive outcomes will occur.", created_at:1779139093, source_id:"chunk-0b07ef4dcf56fe79aaec78af52489ef5", entity_id:"Giving Up Hope"}}, {_id:665, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"UNKNOWN", truncate:"", description:"The shrinking self experiences life as a race due to constant comparison.", created_at:1779139093, source_id:"chunk-0b07ef4dcf56fe79aaec78af52489ef5", entity_id:"Comparison with Others"}}, {_id:666, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"UNKNOWN", truncate:"", description:"Attempting to change behavior, culture, or language to transcend the destructive self.", created_at:1779139093, source_id:"chunk-0b07ef4dcf56fe79aaec78af52489ef5", entity_id:"Rening Behavior"}}, {_id:667, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source", entity_type:"person", truncate:"", created_at:1779184128, description:"Birbal was a witty minister of Akbar who participated in his intellectual challenges.<SEP>Birbal is a witty minister who searches for the biggest fool in the kingdom and later helps an old man find his lost key.<SEP>Birbal is a minister of Akbar who solved the emperor's challenge by identifying the \"biggest fool\" in the kingdom.<SEP>Birbal was a witty minister of Akbar who solved the emperor's challenge by identifying the old man as the fool.<SEP>Birbal was a witty minister to Emperor Akbar who solved a challenge by identifying a fool searching for a lost key under a lamppost.", source_id:"chunk-48d38d40b501a5ac9741fdde5e643c26<SEP>chunk-b66d4da8c241088f7962f1c7ffd83fd6<SEP>chunk-da4b247a4eac03fe686b0059bd126928<SEP>chunk-2a44f8cb9c9f8ea13650035b5bbd408c<SEP>chunk-813e5d6774fbe0673f530d4b67ec6629", entity_id:"Birbal"}}, {_id:668, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2DLb6hDIhmg)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RvgN5Mfbd5A)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Represents the threat posed by the elephant and the broader context of crises requiring caution.<SEP>Danger represents threats that true friends help each other mitigate.", created_at:1779675622, source_id:"chunk-2ed6c538824d03e53845129e9fe68f60<SEP>chunk-f9137367b6fc0c1e310ef8df615fc408", entity_id:"Danger"}}, {_id:669, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source", entity_type:"person", truncate:"", created_at:1779179501, description:"Akbar was the Mughal emperor known for intellectual challenges and debates with his ministers.<SEP>Akbar is the Mughal emperor who posed an intellectual challenge to his ministers, including Birbal.<SEP>Akbar was the Mughal emperor known for intellectual challenges and debates with his ministers.", source_id:"chunk-48d38d40b501a5ac9741fdde5e643c26<SEP>chunk-da4b247a4eac03fe686b0059bd126928<SEP>chunk-2a44f8cb9c9f8ea13650035b5bbd408c", entity_id:"Akbar"}}, {_id:670, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Inertia describes a state of stagnation or lack of progress in addressing deeper personal issues.", created_at:1779139120, source_id:"chunk-48d38d40b501a5ac9741fdde5e643c26", entity_id:"Inertia"}}, {_id:671, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"The biggest fool is a hypothetical or symbolic concept central to Akbar's challenge.", created_at:1779139121, source_id:"chunk-48d38d40b501a5ac9741fdde5e643c26", entity_id:"Biggest Fool"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:`UNIQUE IMPORT LABEL`{`UNIQUE IMPORT ID`: row._id}) SET n += row.properties SET n:base;
UNWIND [{_id:672, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"event", truncate:"", description:"Akbar posed a challenge to his ministers to identify the biggest fool in the kingdom.", created_at:1779139121, source_id:"chunk-48d38d40b501a5ac9741fdde5e643c26", entity_id:"Challenge to Find the Biggest Fool"}}, {_id:673, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"UNKNOWN", truncate:"", description:"Inertia drives desperate actions like gym visits or detox without addressing root causes.", created_at:1779139121, source_id:"chunk-48d38d40b501a5ac9741fdde5e643c26", entity_id:"Desperate Efforts"}}, {_id:674, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"UNKNOWN", truncate:"", description:"True transformation requires conscious acknowledgment of deeper internal conflicts.", created_at:1779139121, source_id:"chunk-48d38d40b501a5ac9741fdde5e643c26", entity_id:"True Transformation"}}, {_id:675, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"The moral of the story illustrates that external solutions often fail to address internal conflicts, emphasizing the need to look within for resolution.", created_at:1779139143, source_id:"chunk-b66d4da8c241088f7962f1c7ffd83fd6", entity_id:"Moral of the Story"}}, {_id:676, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"artifact", truncate:"", description:"The lost key is a physical object that the old man is searching for, located in a dark corner.", created_at:1779139143, source_id:"chunk-b66d4da8c241088f7962f1c7ffd83fd6", entity_id:"The Lost Key"}}, {_id:677, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"person", truncate:"", description:"The emperor asked Birbal to find the biggest fool in the kingdom.", created_at:1779139143, source_id:"chunk-b66d4da8c241088f7962f1c7ffd83fd6", entity_id:"The Emperor"}}, {_id:678, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"The moral of the story illustrates that external solutions often fail to address internal conflicts, emphasizing the need to look within for resolution.", created_at:1779139143, source_id:"chunk-b66d4da8c241088f7962f1c7ffd83fd6", entity_id:"The Moral of the Story"}}, {_id:679, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"person", truncate:"", description:"The old man is searching for his lost key and is found under a dim lamppost.", created_at:1779139143, source_id:"chunk-b66d4da8c241088f7962f1c7ffd83fd6", entity_id:"The Old Man"}}, {_id:681, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Birbal?s story is a reference used to illustrate the difficulty of solving problems by looking inward.", created_at:1779139176, source_id:"chunk-bfc9ac02b4b45204e93a15d51a959bb6", entity_id:"Birbals story"}}, {_id:682, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=M8XASiz30oE)<SEP>YouTube Video: k8iO5daXllM (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=k8iO5daXllM)", entity_type:"person", truncate:"", description:"Entity Name: Partner

Description List:<SEP>A significant other or companion in a personal or professional relationship, referenced in the context of social comparison.", created_at:1779663717, source_id:"chunk-bfc9ac02b4b45204e93a15d51a959bb6<SEP>chunk-2027d5d29fa51b3271fe7bed35b55798<SEP>chunk-326ece98f6d256a814a626f5e89cbf94<SEP>chunk-697da9f4d9cac1cfedd243857a8b8ccc<SEP>chunk-0e5b03097ca1fd70284be6d33317832d<SEP>chunk-924b77c112ecc0d58074213d49a1a3d2<SEP>chunk-4d246f0bbbd6194a476f340fc1b4843e<SEP>chunk-9ce1c80b4cf41412d36baabed73cd0a7<SEP>chunk-8b1cb9338748404cabaa24ac4be68f56<SEP>chunk-52c5f3147f6ff09e1eb20afd47fa7a49<SEP>chunk-33160338b40b6e5d5350d51dafa984b5<SEP>chunk-0fd54b20f9240836a740d21443f8c6ce", entity_id:"Partner"}}, {_id:683, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf", entity_type:"person", truncate:"", description:"The author?s boss is portrayed as taking credit for their work, causing resentment.", created_at:1779139176, source_id:"chunk-bfc9ac02b4b45204e93a15d51a959bb6", entity_id:"Boss"}}, {_id:684, properties:{file_path:"The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kPuvsIyt6UI)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fj2_d2lNGVk)<SEP>YouTube Video: HtmLQkxj8ec (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HtmLQkxj8ec)<SEP>YouTube Video: 38-NgBAet1c (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=38-NgBAet1c)<SEP>YouTube Video: s6B81c2uTGg (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=s6B81c2uTGg)<SEP>YouTube Video: mmpmX3-qfc4 (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mmpmX3-qfc4)<SEP>YouTube Video: Lst4MvxPCx4 (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Lst4MvxPCx4)<SEP>YouTube Video: QzJ_Ft1de1o (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QzJ_Ft1de1o)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=E8N04l1Lptk)", entity_type:"person", truncate:"", description:"We need to parse the input. The entity name is \"Children\". The description list is a JSON list of description objects, each on a new line. However, the input appears to be a JSON object with a key \"Description\" that contains a string that is not a proper JSON list but a description of the list. The description list includes:

