Breath is a physiological process that serves as a tool in meditation to regulate the mind and body, and it is also described as a biological process involving the exchange of gases, specifically oxygen and carbon dioxide. Linked to the mystical concept of Prana (life force), breath regulation through pranayama practices influences consciousness and is associated with achieving states like Swasa, possibly referring to meditative absorption. The journey of breath into and out", source_id:"chunk-70c6bbdb11e53c9f8f6f300d287b2520<SEP>chunk-6ceaf029b184877ef7237e73de7e90eb<SEP>chunk-5a1740daf11f031bb2f4e4877b90a316<SEP>chunk-e2d0ff9dea6a5334fbc3569bce6e4413<SEP>chunk-e15affa7e924b9530baaf1cc0152bad4<SEP>chunk-d887f374fce140e42345a26a703cd352<SEP>chunk-3198061b7d9cb7c891cdfe291494700c<SEP>chunk-7234398961838f3894f5b3cb8bdb630b<SEP>chunk-369c95aae7fc4dbe0b27e0f7e8e427f7<SEP>chunk-ac91c3a51bfc466fbc02960659f7837d<SEP>chunk-5bf3950956a6b9404d15a3583f147386", entity_id:"Breath"}}] AS row
