focus of the described practices and exercises.", source_id:"chunk-6254a0998449b5aae9f36e202e6ddd4f<SEP>chunk-f82fe879a5991d902752f3c7f1e83fb7<SEP>chunk-dd06aca0e8b0e45b68bcb022e995fab4<SEP>chunk-510c74de625674a35dffb4f0f8a8acb0<SEP>chunk-2946fd6f690a4f147698b0825594b6df", entity_id:"Mental Health"}}, {_id:2001, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=B8wapoLAu84)<SEP>YouTube Video: Vr3PS2DdbDU (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Vr3PS2DdbDU)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Tc8f9ZasRRM)", entity_type:"naturalobject", truncate:"", created_at:1779673193, description:"The prefrontal cortex is a brain region that can be engaged to shift activity from the amygdala, enabling logical thinking. It is the part of the brain where logical thinking occurs, and activity can be shifted from the amygdala to this region. The prefrontal cortex is a brain region involved in executive functions such as decision-making and moderating social behavior. It is also the brain region responsible for conscious decision-making and positive thinking. Additionally, the prefrontal cortex is associated with higher-order thinking and decision-making, as well as intelligence and cognitive functions. It is a brain region that is mentioned in the context of blood flow effects, with increased blood flow noted.

Overall, the prefrontal cortex is a key area for logical, executive, and social functions, and it is linked to intelligence and blood flow changes.<SEP>The prefrontal cortex is mentioned as a brain region where increased blood flow enhances intelligence.<SEP>The prefrontal cortex is mentioned as a brain region where increased blood flow enhances intelligence.<SEP>Brain region associated with intelligence and cognitive functions, mentioned in the context of increased blood flow.<SEP>The prefrontal cortex is a part of the brain involved in intelligence and relationships.<SEP>The prefrontal cortex is a part of the brain associated with intelligence, which experiences increased blood flow during the practice.", source_id:"chunk-6254a0998449b5aae9f36e202e6ddd4f<SEP>chunk-f82fe879a5991d902752f3c7f1e83fb7<SEP>chunk-510c74de625674a35dffb4f0f8a8acb0<SEP>chunk-22f4f001e75bdf8bb249d6c2ed547355<SEP>chunk-019177d585b65eb10f97dfb309cde652<SEP>chunk-53e525d93caa11247db9588a7b9a8e7a<SEP>chunk-fb4ec1b021168c6010bcec1085967625<SEP>chunk-4e775b554bb52f0e7b422520123fe5a4<SEP>chunk-a806b7026395d82c6e1fe100191449c6<SEP>chunk-9174f4aac6278b492855cabdc7a615b1<SEP>chunk-6cf55136aa5e4ce74dabd0e6bc9c5c31", entity_id:"Prefrontal Cortex"}}, {_id:2003, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=B8wapoLAu84)<SEP>YouTube Video: igSp4H0OWLE (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=igSp4H0OWLE)<SEP>YouTube Video: k0GsZxWhjSE (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=k0GsZxWhjSE)", entity_type:"naturalobject", truncate:"", created_at:1779552331, description:"<think>
