d as having a different philosophical focus compared to modern civilization.<SEP>Ancient Indians explored a unique philosophical question about self-identity and consciousness.", created_at:1779554093, source_id:"chunk-2d3e2b583a33b1dd3f28054d2d3f1c75<SEP>chunk-0cbe1e9a1fff09e96a2f2e778a059a9c<SEP>chunk-833c73287ea461916c12ac0516e36f74<SEP>chunk-b45f3a725ee597bc7f79c1f42e7fee1d", entity_id:"Ancient Indians"}}, {_id:2224, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_XDcXdBDZ0c)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Eating with sacredness involves consuming food only when genuinely hungry, not out of temptation, as practiced by ancient Indians.", created_at:1779164341, source_id:"chunk-2d3e2b583a33b1dd3f28054d2d3f1c75", entity_id:"Eating with Sacredness"}}, {_id:2225, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_XDcXdBDZ0c)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Engaging in acts like a duty refers to performing actions mechanically without deep connection or sacredness.", created_at:1779164341, source_id:"chunk-2d3e2b583a33b1dd3f28054d2d3f1c75", entity_id:"Engaging in Acts Like a Duty"}}] AS row
