UNWIND [{_id:2722, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source", entity_type:"person", truncate:"", description:"A fish seller who used the flower seller?s flower basket to fall asleep, overcoming the stench of her own fish.", created_at:1779179023, source_id:"chunk-d4fb27ed500b1a960390eadd6d011176", entity_id:"Fish Seller"}}, {_id:2723, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Chaotic thinking represents a mental state of overwhelming, disorganized thoughts that hinder clarity and progress.`", created_at:1779179024, source_id:"chunk-b75e52bdeada1ddd1aebcff0a658afb0", entity_id:"Chaotic Thinking"}}, {_id:2724, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Joyful honesty reflects unfiltered emotional expression without fear of judgment, characteristic of the Happy Child state.`", created_at:1779179024, source_id:"chunk-b75e52bdeada1ddd1aebcff0a658afb0", entity_id:"Joyful Honesty"}}, {_id:2725, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source", entity_type:"UNKNOWN", truncate:"", description:"Rick Hanson?s work explains how repetitive emotions shape neural connections.", created_at:1779179148, source_id:"chunk-d4fb27ed500b1a960390eadd6d011176", entity_id:"neuroplasticity"}}, {_id:2726, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: RGFI6v2Biq0 (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RGFI6v2Biq0)", entity_type:"artifact", truncate:"", created_at:1779510881, description:"Hindu temples feature diverse imagery, representing the totality of human experience, including both positive and negative emotions.<SEP>The Hindu temple symbolizes the totality of human experience, featuring both sacred and ordinary elements like gods, daily life, and demons.<SEP>The Hindu temple serves as a metaphor for the human mind, containing images of deities, daily life, and provocative postures to symbolize the totality of human consciousness.", source_id:"chunk-1444d9544f5a6ff9532dfcc5227c350f<SEP>chunk-21bacf187c7f2b778c240499081154ba<SEP>chunk-c2f772787ab946a352d0af09f5686d4b<SEP>chunk-edcb79b79435bcba9facfbb3e2e5ae09", entity_id:"Hindu Temple"}}, {_id:2727, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hcNDrMy6gCE)<SEP>YouTube Video: 1_-cZz8YRFw (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1_-cZz8YRFw)<SEP>YouTube Video: 1PlGMOAypCI (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1PlGMOAypCI)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", created_at:1779655475, description:"Guilt is an emotional state experienced by Diego following his son's death, stemming from his perceived responsibility and inability to connect with his son.<SEP>Guilt is a state that Diego fell into, believing it was a way to love his son, but was actually a form of self-punishment.<SEP>An emotion parents are advised to overcome for healthy relationships.`<SEP>Guilt is an emotional state arising from remorse over actions or failures, contributing to Dasharatha's torment and eventual demise.<SEP>Guilt is an emotional state discussed in the context of forgiveness, with Krishnaji rejecting its worship.<SEP>Guilt is a concept discussed in the text.<SEP>Guilt is an emotion experienced by Peter after denying Jesus.", source_id:"chunk-214089f71bed8468f80247a24979283e<SEP>chunk-999192b96103e7c498639cfadd062722<SEP>chunk-938d8c7cf2e140a4e60de3b5d9b45278<SEP>chunk-c0b80dedb75ca2eb809b280546928f57<SEP>chunk-48c6db0a5b206ddf4f5b6555c5408117<SEP>chunk-96ee5b32030dd42df75feab094827373<SEP>chunk-51a2b155e4eeb45d726ca7ab16117dcc", entity_id:"Guilt"}}, {_id:2728, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source", entity_type:"event", truncate:"", description:"Talent Search Competitions are events Diego plans to organize in his son's memory to promote young talent and serve as a tribute.<SEP>Annual talent search competitions are an initiative Diego decided to hold in memory of his son, aiming to promote his son's love for being a DJ.", created_at:1779183930, source_id:"chunk-214089f71bed8468f80247a