fers to the perception of distinctions between individuals or groups, leading to division.", created_at:1779232027, source_id:"chunk-c69cfc9260a595202e649b77a2983253", entity_id:"Difference"}}, {_id:3512, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AB-t5CoxMHM)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mNM-x9RFMcE)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Sickness is paired with disease to emphasize the mental health implications of division.<SEP>Sickness encompasses health issues faced by medical workers, including fatigue and mask-related discomfort.", created_at:1779257852, source_id:"chunk-ce09b6c6a2ea185889fd9682aa9fd726<SEP>chunk-1c356513974368f71d2bdbafe2a1f92d", entity_id:"Sickness"}}, {_id:3513, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"sankalpa mudranau refers to a spiritual practice involving palm placement and conscious breathing.", created_at:1779232601, source_id:"chunk-37d176f97b7ba2ae42fdf4ae41e9150e", entity_id:"sankalpa mudranau"}}, {_id:3514, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"antir yamin describes a divine presence within the heart, referenced in the spiritual guidance.", created_at:1779232601, source_id:"chunk-37d176f97b7ba2ae42fdf4ae41e9150e", entity_id:"antir yamin"}}, {_id:3515, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source", entity_type:"location", truncate:"", description:"puja room is a designated space for spiritual practices mentioned in the instructions.", created_at:1779232601, source_id:"chunk-37d176f97b7ba2ae42fdf4ae41e9150e", entity_id:"puja room"}}, {_id:3516, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"kangalpa is a term related to spiritual intentions or resolutions, repeatedly emphasized in the text.", created_at:1779232601, source_id:"chunk-37d176f97b7ba2ae42fdf4ae41e9150e", entity_id:"kangalpa"}}, {_id:3518, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UbCEX5KBbPw)<SEP>YouTube Video: nQpRoOOu5Yc (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nQpRoOOu5Yc)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Chaitra Masa is the first month of the Hindu lunar calendar, associated with Ugadi celebrations.<SEP>Chaitra Masa is the lunar calendar month during which Ugadi is celebrated, corresponding to April in the Gregorian calendar.<SEP>Chaitra Masa is the lunar month in the Hindu calendar during which Ugadi is celebrated.<SEP>Chaitra Masa is the first month of the Hindu lunar calendar, associated with Ugadi celebrations and cyclical timekeeping.", created_at:1779519051, source_id:"chunk-4ab4bc9db393a14f0ecfea6c76d9e372<SEP>chunk-61d286a10ba0271970a579e1cf354cf5<SEP>chunk-6af3220a340f626ce621832ca3542da1<SEP>chunk-f34e8e10dbf92b5936295383ee0c7f10", entity_id:"Chaitra Masa"}}, {_id:3520, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UbCEX5KBbPw)", entity_type:"artifact", truncate:"", description:"Bevubella is the South Indian name for Ugadi Pachadi, representing life's flavors.<SEP>Bevubella is another name for Ugadi Pachadi, a dish symbolizing life's diverse tastes in South Indian culture.", created_at:1779232745, source_id:"chunk-4ab4bc9db393a14f0ecfea6c76d9e372<SEP>chunk-61c739c46e4f6213506db20ff0e52508", entity_id:"Bevubella"}}, {_id:3522, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UbCEX5KBbPw)", entity_type:"artifact", truncate:"", created_at:1779518974, description:"Ugadi Pachadi is a traditional dish consumed during Ugadi, symbolizing life's diverse experiences.<SEP>Ugadi Pachadi (Bevubella) is a traditional dish prepared during Ugadi, containing a mix of flavors representing life's experiences.<SEP>Ugadi Pachadi is a dish made of various ingredients, symbolizing the different tastes of life.", source_id:"chunk-4ab4bc9db393a14f0ecfea6c76d9e372<SEP>chunk-61c739c46e4f6213506db20ff0e52508<SEP>chunk-6af3220a340f626ce621832ca3542da1", entity_id:"Ugadi Pachadi"}}, {_id:3524, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Ugadi Sankalpa is a spiritual resolution or vow taken during the Ugadi festival, associated with intentions for the new year.", created_at:1779232602, source_id:"chunk-6b7fcb0be46e5dc8bc514960fa89b8be", entity_id:"Ugadi Sankalpa"}}, {_id:3526, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source", entity_type:"artifact", truncate:"", description:"Surya Yantra Mandala is a symbolic or actual structure representing the sun's energy, integral to Ekam's design and power.", created_at:1779232603, source_id:"chunk-6b7fcb0be46e5dc8bc514960fa89b8be", entity_id:"Surya Yantra Mandala"}}, {_id:3531, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source", entity_type:"event", truncate:"", description:"Sunset is one of the four cardinal times when Ekam is most powerful.", created_at:1779232604, source_id:"chunk-6b7fcb0be46e5dc8bc514960fa89b8be", entity_id:"Sunset"}}, {_id:3532, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source", entity_type:"event", truncate:"", description:"Sunrise is one of the four cardinal times when Ekam is most powerful.", created_at:1779232604, source_id:"chunk-6b7fcb0be46e5dc8bc514960fa89b8be", entity_id:"Sunrise"}}, {_id:3533, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source", entity_type:"event", truncate:"", description:"Midday is one of the four cardinal times when Ekam is most powerful.", created_at:1779232604, source_id:"chunk-6b7fcb0be46e5dc8bc514960fa89b8be", entity_id:"Midday"}}, {_id:3534, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source", entity_type:"event", truncate:"", description:"Midnight is one of the four cardinal times when Ekam is most powerful.", created_at:1779232604, source_id:"chunk-6b7fcb0be46e5dc8bc514960fa89b8be", entity_id:"Midnight"}}, {_id:3535, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Antharyamina is the inner self or inner divine presence that the mantra connects to.", created_at:1779232604, source_id:"chunk-6b7fcb0be46e5dc8bc514960fa89b8be", entity_id:"Antharyamina"}}, {_id:3536, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UbCEX5KBbPw)", entity_type:"event", truncate:"", description:"Ugadi (also called Yugadi or Gudipadwa) is a festival celebrated on the first day of the lunar Chaitra Masa, symbolizing new beginnings and cyclical renewal.", created_at:1779232716, source_id:"chunk-61d286a10ba0271970a579e1cf354cf5", entity_id:"Ugadi/Yugadi/Gudipadwa"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:`UNIQUE IMPORT LABEL`{`UNIQUE IMPORT ID`: row._id}) SET n += row.properties SET n:base;
UNWIND [{_id:3537, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UbCEX5KBbPw)", entity_type:"artifact", truncate:"", description:"Ugadi Pachadi (called Bevubella in the south) is a traditional dish symbolizing life's diverse experiences through its mixed flavors.", created_at:1779232716, source_id:"chunk-61d286a10ba0271970a579e1cf354cf5", entity_id:"Ugadi Pachadi/Bevubella"}}, {_id:3538, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UbCEX5KBbPw)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Sthita prajna tava describes a state of spiritual awakening characterized by equanimity in all life experiences.", created_at:1779232716, source_id:"chunk-61d286a10ba0271970a579e1cf354cf5", entity_id:"Sthita Prajna Tava"}}, {_id:3539, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UbCEX5KBbPw)", entity_type:"category", truncate:"", description:"April 13th is the specific date for Ugadi celebrations in the Gregorian calendar for this year.", created_at:1779232716, source_id:"chunk-61d286a10ba0271970a579e1cf354cf5", entity_id:"April 13th"}}, {_id:3540, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UbCEX5KBbPw)<SEP>YouTube Video: nQpRoOOu5Yc (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nQpRoOOu5Yc)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"The universe is described as cyclical, contracting and expanding endlessly as part of its fundamental nature.<SEP>The cyclical universe theory posits endless contraction and expansion, mirrored in biological and psychological processes.", created_at:1779519051, source_id:"chunk-61d286a10ba0271970a579e1cf354cf5<SEP>chunk-f34e8e10dbf92b5936295383ee0c7f10", entity_id:"Cyclical Universe"}}, {_id:3541, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UbCEX5KBbPw)", entity_type:"method", truncate:"", description:"Sankalpa mudra is a ritual gesture involving placing the right palm over the left, symbolizing inner connection.", created_at:1779232745, source_id:"chunk-61c739c46e4f6213506db20ff0e52508", entity_id:"Sankalpa Mudra"}}, {_id:3542, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UbCEX5KBbPw)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"The shloka \"Avarthano nivruthatma samvruta sampramardhanaha\" emphasizes cyclicality and divine liberation in life's challenges.", created_at:1779232745, source_id:"chunk-61c739c46e4f6213506db20ff0e52508", entity_id:"Shloka"}}, {_id:3543, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UbCEX5KBbPw)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"The divine represents the ultimate power and source of cyclicality and liberation in life, as described in the shloka.", created_at:1779232745, source_id:"chunk-61c739c46e4f6213506db20ff0e52508", entity_id:"the divine"}}, {_id:3544, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UbCEX5KBbPw)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Adira is a state of being that the speaker aims to embody.", created_at:1779232792, source_id:"chunk-ad4544e5cec6ee250e4823e5b924afdf", entity_id:"Adira"}}, {_id:3545, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UbCEX5KBbPw)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Sthita Prajna is a state of being that the speaker aims to embody.", created_at:1779232792, source_id:"chunk-ad4544e5cec6ee250e4823e5b924afdf", entity_id:"Sthita Prajna"}}, {_id:3546, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zCnqQBfyXa4)<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jy4hcpUSBms)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Rajas is a concept in Hindu philosophy representing aggression and energy.<SEP>Rajas is a quality of aggression that the seeker must overcome with the grace of Maha Lakshmi.<SEP>Rajas represents the quality of restlessness and craving, one of the three gunas.` -> Correct.<SEP>Rajas is a term that was corrected to be capitalized.", created_at:1779673433, source_id:"chunk-f53df8caed63deff1ec1228640c8a22a<SEP>chunk-ae85e43970032506c9fc6caf0b0538ed<SEP>chunk-06509bca67cf9977473996911215a1e2<SEP>chunk-a7efc3b9dab03e6e433daab7a3b11310<SEP>chunk-f4789be1157bad19695ee05e51925d91", entity_id:"Rajas"}}, {_id:3547, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zCnqQBfyXa4)<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jy4hcpUSBms)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", created_at:1779673384, description:"Tamas is a concept in Hindu philosophy symbolizing inertia and darkness.<SEP>Tamas is a quality of darkness that the seeker must overcome with the grace of Goddess Durga.<SEP>Tamas refers to the state of darkness, inertia, and ignorance in consciousness, dispelled through spiritual practices during Navratri.`<SEP>...` -> Correct.<SEP>Tamas symbolizes darkness, laziness, and ignorance, the third guna.` -> Correct.<SEP>Tamas signifies dark qualities like laziness, anger, and greed in the scripture.", source_id:"chunk-f53df8caed63deff1ec1228640c8a22a<SEP>chunk-ae85e43970032506c9fc6caf0b0538ed<SEP>chunk-672a64891a721958057240b2cc83a897<SEP>chunk-06509bca67cf9977473996911215a1e2<SEP>chunk-a7efc3b9dab03e6e433daab7a3b11310", entity_id:"Tamas"}}, {_id:3548, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zCnqQBfyXa4)<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jy4hcpUSBms)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Sattva is a concept in Hindu philosophy denoting purity, balance, and a state of flow.<SEP>Sattva is a state of flow characterized by the absence of agitation and associated with positive emotions like love, peace, joy, and gratitude.<SEP>Sattva is a state of calmness and contentment, one of the three gunas (qualities) in Hindu philosophy.` -> Correct.<SEP>Sattva represents a spiritual quality symbolizing purity and balance in the scripture.<SEP>Sattva is a concept related to being calm and contented, and is part of a seeker's journey.<SEP>Sattva is a quality of calm and contentment.<SEP>Sattva represents a state of calmness, contentment, and freedom from desire, often associated with spiritual equilibrium.", created_at:1779675419, source_id:"chunk-f53df8caed63deff1ec1228640c8a22a<SEP>chunk-c7f811687ac2ecce0042e89dfc14b5e5<SEP>chunk-06509bca67cf9977473996911215a1e2<SEP>chunk-a7efc3b9dab03e6e433daab7a3b11310<SEP>chunk-f4789be1157bad19695ee05e51925d91<SEP>chunk-0d847b42bbc0f3e13f07c034a5c8e0d1<SEP>chunk-05cc795d538216c463ac6d6e2524a3ee", entity_id:"Sattva"}}, {_id:3549, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zCnqQBfyXa4)", entity_type:"UNKNOWN", truncate:"", description:"Sattva is associated with positive emotional states and aspects of consciousness.", created_at:1779234152, source_id:"chunk-c7f811687ac2ecce0042e89dfc14b5e5", entity_id:"love, peace, joy, gratitude"}}, {_id:3550, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zCnqQBfyXa4)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=owXqW04b08o)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Christian Christian is listed as a participant in the source text.<SEP>A repeated word in the mantra context, identified as a transcription error.", created_at:1779241048, source_id:"chunk-181fe00b0fce4add5c4bbbdb6823978c<SEP>chunk-6195ca7f73d379cf72b6e612c1bd422a", entity_id:"Christian Christian"}}, {_id:3558, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hcNDrMy6gCE)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", created_at:1779240822, description:"Gayatri Mantra is a specific term of art that was correctly identified.<SEP>The Gayatri Mantra is a sacred Hindu mantra associated with the goddess Gayatri and used in Vedic rituals.<SEP>The Gayatri Mantra is referenced as a clearer version of the garbled text.", source_id:"chunk-1c73a5c2c2a2898e93a8be652417081d<SEP>chunk-ded082abd496ba4dd1acaf011d64e44c<SEP>chunk-398e965cd8ff044e9710f53404b93961", entity_id:"Gayatri Mantra"}}, {_id:3560, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hcNDrMy6gCE)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Brahmopadesha is a specific term of art that was correctly identified.<SEP>Brahmopadesha refers to the traditional Hindu practice of spiritual initiation and knowledge transmission from teacher to student.<SEP>The corrected term for \"Brahmopadesham,\" indicating a spiritual teaching or instruction.<SEP>Corrected domain-specific term for a ritual or knowledge transmission from mother to daughter.", created_at:1779235170, source_id:"chunk-1c73a5c2c2a2898e93a8be652417081d<SEP>chunk-ded082abd496ba4dd1acaf011d64e44c<SEP>chunk-3d9c3392a3fb94c3fb2e7b6067f50fe9<SEP>chunk-8d8816024cb91617d5b95e26e35016b6", entity_id:"Brahmopadesha"}}, {_id:3561, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"achared is a misquoted term that was corrected to \"acharet\".", created_at:1779234597, source_id:"chunk-1c73a5c2c2a2898e93a8be652417081d", entity_id:"achared"}}, {_id:3562, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Preety Ji is the correct spelling for the term \"Preethaji\".", created_at:1779234597, source_id:"chunk-1c73a5c2c2a2898e93a8be652417081d", entity_id:"Preety Ji"}}, {_id:3563, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: YguId6pF5KI (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YguId6pF5KI)<SEP>YouTube Video: DmzZPgTh7_M (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DmzZPgTh7_M)<SEP>YouTube Video: YkIBYppBtro (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YkIBYppBtro)", entity_type:"person", truncate:"", created_at:1779565425, description:"Krishna Ji is the correct spelling for the term \"Krishnaji\".<SEP>Krishna Ji is a revered teacher and leader known for his structured teachings on consciousness, lived authenticity, and guiding participants toward awakened states.<SEP>Krishna Ji is a spiritual leader known for his teachings, guidance, and embodiment of truthful, calm, and loving principles.<SEP>A spiritual figure referenced in the text, collaborating with Akam to challenge traditional gender norms in spirituality.<SEP>Krishna Ji is a spiritual teacher who discusses enlightenment and happiness, addressing students and the challenges of the hungry mind.<SEP>Krishna Ji is a spiritual teacher who discusses enlightenment and happiness, addressing students and the challenges of the hungry mind.<SEP>Krishna ji is a person addressed in the context of high expectations and stress.", source_id:"chunk-1c73a5c2c2a2898e93a8be652417081d<SEP>chunk-ea6ac06a0214aa495f14ca8162f76be3<SEP>chunk-d078b842a118a3665da45a82508e955c<SEP>chunk-62d9c2c61a7070c1d594767ed9814cde<SEP>chunk-bdaca57c11a3d551259155ef196cf16d<SEP>chunk-f87f1002a8699b889bcce1050f8f041d<SEP>chunk-6beab04bb204a738c7bc57c3d444cb13", entity_id:"Krishna Ji"}}, {_id:3564, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source", entity_type:"UNKNOWN", truncate:"", description:"The term \"achared\" was corrected to \"acharet\".", created_at:1779234639, source_id:"chunk-1c73a5c2c2a2898e93a8be652417081d", entity_id:"acharet"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:`UNIQUE IMPORT LABEL`{`UNIQUE IMPORT ID`: row._id}) SET n += row.properties SET n:base;
UNWIND [{_id:3565, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hcNDrMy6gCE)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Lalayet pancha varshani is a Sanskrit phrase meaning \"shower as much love as you can on the child until five years old,\" used in the text to emphasize child-rearing principles.<SEP>A Sanskrit phrase from Vedic sages meaning \"shower as much love as you can on the child until five years old.\"", created_at:1779234827, source_id:"chunk-65fa0d837a6f9738c2577370123f7d08<SEP>chunk-2192624c5b62e2be4b1843e100b2178a", entity_id:"Lalayet Pancha Varshani"}}, {_id:3571, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hcNDrMy6gCE)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"A grammatical error involving redundant phrasing (\"or don't allow\") that disrupts sentence flow.", created_at:1779234827, source_id:"chunk-2192624c5b62e2be4b1843e100b2178a", entity_id:"Repetition in \"or Don't Allow\""}}, {_id:3573, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hcNDrMy6gCE)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"The revised phrasing to eliminate redundancy and improve clarity in the sentence.", created_at:1779234827, source_id:"chunk-2192624c5b62e2be4b1843e100b2178a", entity_id:"Corrected Repetition: \"or Allow Your Children\""}}, {_id:3574, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hcNDrMy6gCE)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"The corrected version of the sentence that adheres to grammatical rules, emphasizing collective action in parenting.", created_at:1779234827, source_id:"chunk-2192624c5b62e2be4b1843e100b2178a", entity_id:"Together, You Sculpt Your Child's Destiny"}}, {_id:3575, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hcNDrMy6gCE)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"A grammatical adjustment to replace \"last their entire lifetime\" with \"last for their entire lifetime\" for better idiomatic expression.", created_at:1779234827, source_id:"chunk-2192624c5b62e2be4b1843e100b2178a", entity_id:"Idiomatic Correction for \"Last Their Entire Lifetime\""}}, {_id:3576, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hcNDrMy6gCE)", entity_type:"organization", truncate:"", description:"Ancient scholars cited in the text for their wisdom on parenting and child-rearing practices.", created_at:1779234827, source_id:"chunk-2192624c5b62e2be4b1843e100b2178a", entity_id:"Vedic Sages"}}, {_id:3577, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hcNDrMy6gCE)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"A grammatical error in the original text where the phrasing \"It is by together you sculpt...\" is incorrect and needs correction to improve readability and punctuation.", created_at:1779234827, source_id:"chunk-2192624c5b62e2be4b1843e100b2178a", entity_id:"It Is By Together You Sculpt..."}}, {_id:3578, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hcNDrMy6gCE)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"The translated meaning of the Sanskrit phrase emphasizing unconditional love for children under five.", created_at:1779234828, source_id:"chunk-2192624c5b62e2be4b1843e100b2178a", entity_id:"Shower as Much Love"}}, {_id:3579, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hcNDrMy6gCE)", entity_type:"UNKNOWN", truncate:"", description:"\"last their entire lifetime\" is corrected to \"last for their entire lifetime\" for proper idiomatic usage.", created_at:1779234828, source_id:"chunk-2192624c5b62e2be4b1843e100b2178a", entity_id:"Last Their Entire Lifetime"}}, {_id:3580, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hcNDrMy6gCE)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"age 6 to 16 years is a temporal range referenced in the context of the Sanskrit phrase \"dashavarshani thadayet,\" interpreted as a period during which one should wait or hold.", created_at:1779234849, source_id:"chunk-2723258b7583662b093307188081c1b7", entity_id:"age 6 to 16 years"}}, {_id:3581, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hcNDrMy6gCE)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Sanskrit phrase \"dashavarshani thadayet\" (???????? ????????), interpreted as \"one should wait/hold\" in the context of ages 6-16, with \"dashavarshani\" meaning \"ten-year-old\" and \"thadayet\" meaning \"to wait/hold\".", created_at:1779234849, source_id:"chunk-2723258b7583662b093307188081c1b7", entity_id:"dashavarshani thadayet"}}, {_id:3582, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hcNDrMy6gCE)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Nurturing beautiful states like gratitude, compassion, kindness, joyfulness, and courage in children during ages 6-16.", created_at:1779234892, source_id:"chunk-919e07d8805901037c461f19cf5f869e", entity_id:"Nurturing Beautiful States"}}, {_id:3583, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hcNDrMy6gCE)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"The metaphor comparing a child to a garden during ages 6-16, emphasizing cultivation of positive qualities.", created_at:1779234892, source_id:"chunk-919e07d8805901037c461f19cf5f869e", entity_id:"Child as Garden"}}, {_id:3584, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hcNDrMy6gCE)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"A parenting advice against making children feel guilty for not feeling grateful, as mentioned in the context.", created_at:1779234892, source_id:"chunk-919e07d8805901037c461f19cf5f869e", entity_id:"Make Them Feel Bad"}}, {_id:3585, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.c