UNWIND [{_id:3988, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=obK5uqYXOJU)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"A symbolic personification of Earth as a nurturing and wise entity, serving as a role model for sustainable coexistence.<SEP>Grandmother Earth is a metaphorical entity symbolizing the Earth's nurturing and generative qualities.<SEP>Grandmother Earth is a personified representation of Earth, symbolizing the planet's role in sustaining life and cultural development.<SEP>A personified representation of Earth, symbolizing its role in sustaining life and fostering cultural connections.<SEP>Grandmother Earth is referenced as a wise role model in the quote.", created_at:1779250568, source_id:"chunk-6586d0e1f5d54248cb5be73a7d3a343a<SEP>chunk-bb29e2ed1d32a5cd538be88c0d484668<SEP>chunk-d10d3062cabaaccfc33ac170d7845177<SEP>chunk-29504d0af63a387f3edf40d4bb13cddc<SEP>chunk-dde44c38c2ed591da5c942450d84385e", entity_id:"Grandmother Earth"}}, {_id:3989, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=obK5uqYXOJU)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Ancient organisms buried in the ocean depths transformed into fossil fuels over millions of years, originally supporting life while alive.<SEP>Decomposed creatures are ancient organic life forms transformed into fossil fuels over millennia.<SEP>Decomposed creatures include bugs, birds, mammals, reptiles, plants, and trees that lived once and were buried under the sea, later transformed into fossil fuels.<SEP>Decomposed creatures refer to organic matter from decomposed organisms that contribute to energy production and sustainability.<SEP>Decomposed organic matter that contributes to manufacturing processes and everyday living through Mother Earth's womb.", created_at:1779251620, source_id:"chunk-6586d0e1f5d54248cb5be73a7d3a343a<SEP>chunk-bb29e2ed1d32a5cd538be88c0d484668<SEP>chunk-d10d3062cabaaccfc33ac170d7845177<SEP>chunk-c3c5777bd0aa108885f3e118f2c5486c<SEP>chunk-69f7a386fbc619738707246584cb8e2a", entity_id:"Decomposed Creatures"}}, {_id:3990, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=obK5uqYXOJU)", entity_type:"location", truncate:"", created_at:1779250722, description:"The Mariana Trench is the deepest part of the world's oceans, characterized by extreme pressure and hosting unique deep-sea ecosystems.<SEP>The Mariana Trench is the deepest part of the world's oceans, known for extreme pressure and unique ecosystems.<SEP>The Mariana Trench is the deepest part of the world's oceans, located in the western Pacific Ocean.<SEP>The Mariana Trench is the deepest part of the world's oceans, known for extreme pressure conditions and unique survival of living forms.<SEP>The Mariana Trench is the deepest part of the world's oceans, located in the western Pacific Ocean.<SEP>The Mariana Trench is a deep ocean region mentioned in the text, noted for extreme pressure and survival conditions.", source_id:"chunk-6586d0e1f5d54248cb5be73a7d3a343a<SEP>chunk-bb29e2ed1d32a5cd538be88c0d484668<SEP>chunk-4565491a2f82c499948bc59bd08ceda8<SEP>chunk-3fc0440bd350f3b05bf870c0f550544d<SEP>chunk-29504d0af63a387f3edf40d4bb13cddc<SEP>chunk-aa631ec77524d5dc982872db79e03f58", entity_id:"Mariana Trench"}}, {_id:3991, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=obK5uqYXOJU)", entity_type:"naturalobject", truncate:"", created_at:1779251881, description:"Fossil fuels are energy resources formed from the remains of ancient organisms over millions of years. They consist of hydrocarbons derived from decomposed organic matter, which were buried under the sea or the Earth's surface, resulting in their formation.

These fuels serve as primary energy sources for modern industrial processes, transportation, and the powering of human activities. They are currently central to global energy systems, providing the bulk of energy used worldwide.

Fossil fuels are non-renewable, meaning they cannot be replenished within a human timescale. Their extraction and combustion contribute to environmental strain, including greenhouse gas emissions and other pollutants, leading to targeted reductions in sustainability practices.

Despite their importance, the reliance on fossil fuels is being increasingly scrutinized, with efforts to transition toward renewable energy sources to mitigate environmental impacts and address sustainability concerns.<SEP>Fossil fuels are non-renewable energy sources derived from Earth's resources, linked to environmental strain.<SEP>Fossil fuels are non-renewable energy sources derived from decomposed organic matter, used for energy production and daily activities.", source_id:"chunk-6586d0e1f5d54248cb5be73a7d3a343a<SEP>chunk-bb29e2ed1d32a5cd538be88c0d484668<SEP>chunk-4565491a2f82c499948bc59bd08ceda8<SEP>chunk-d10d3062cabaaccfc33ac170d7845177<SEP>chunk-29504d0af63a387f3edf40d4bb13cddc<SEP>chunk-323533a8c8c6c9eda38d56c56d637777<SEP>chunk-7c57553df2850654b5a35e1ee26c7149<SEP>chunk-c3c5777bd0aa108885f3e118f2c5486c<SEP>chunk-b83c8b00df8935f2c00062b416bf9b2c<SEP>chunk-e1984cc91b0da578d9648e1604a3db60", entity_id:"Fossil Fuels"}}, {_id:3992, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=obK5uqYXOJU)", entity_type:"creature", truncate:"", created_at:1779250722, description:"Bar-headed geese are migratory birds known for flying over high-altitude Himalayan ranges, showcasing remarkable endurance.<SEP>Bar-headed geese are migratory birds capable of flying over high altitudes like the Himalayas.<SEP>Bar-headed geese are migratory birds known for flying over the Himalayas during their seasonal migrations.<SEP>Bar-headed geese are mentioned as flying over high altitudes, associated with survival in extreme conditions.", source_id:"chunk-6586d0e1f5d54248cb5be73a7d3a343a<SEP>chunk-bb29e2ed1d32a5cd538be88c0d484668<SEP>chunk-4565491a2f82c499948bc59bd08ceda8<SEP>chunk-aa631ec77524d5dc982872db79e03f58", entity_id:"Bar-headed Geese"}}, {_id:3993, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=obK5uqYXOJU)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"One Earth Citiz