 Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=207izZBbqVg)", entity_type:"UNKNOWN", truncate:"", description:"Corrected punctuation in the sentence.", created_at:1779259733, source_id:"chunk-c072e5291bc196493af69ebd61f4717e", entity_id:"You may slowly open your eyes."}}, {_id:4240, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=207izZBbqVg)", entity_type:"UNKNOWN", truncate:"", description:"Corrections made to the repetition to ensure consistent capitalization.", created_at:1779259733, source_id:"chunk-c072e5291bc196493af69ebd61f4717e", entity_id:"Pree Pree Pree Pree Pree Pree Pree Pree"}}, {_id:4241, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=207izZBbqVg)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", created_at:1779259879, description:"Mantra phrases such as \"Bhakta Priyam, Bhakti Gamyam, Bhakta N?m Kirti Vardhikam, Bhavak Priyam, Satim Devim Vandetvam, Bhakta Vatsalam, Annapurnam, Sadapurnam, Parvati, Parvap\" used during the Upasana ritual for visualization and chanting.<SEP>A list of Sanskrit phrases used in meditation practice, including terms like \"Parvatim Parvapujitam\" and \"Shambhu Shaktim Vandetvam,\" intended for spiritual contemplation.", source_id:"chunk-c87bd389c5c5a0aa7ee00af0f32f42e6<SEP>chunk-8b24420a54f14344af97a060057521ed<SEP>chunk-2e98fa36d7235c33584ec813d1767281", entity_id:"Mantra Phrases"}}, {_id:4256, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=207izZBbqVg)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Dark Space in Front of Closed Eyes describes the meditative focus point during spiritual contemplation.<SEP>Descriptive phrase referring to the dark space in front of one's closed eyes, part of the mantra.", created_at:1779259954, source_id:"chunk-8b24420a54f14344af97a060057521ed<SEP>chunk-521ddf24bfc548a5754de0c8b7f6c963", entity_id:"Dark Space in Front of Closed Eyes"}}, {_id:4257, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=207izZBbqVg)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"An instructional directive guiding practitioners to engage in dharana by visualizing a form within the chidakasha or dark space.<SEP>A directive to perform a meditation practice involving visualization of \"her form in chidakasha\" (inner space) or \"dark space in front of closed eyes.\"", created_at:1779259879, source_id:"chunk-ff46b53ab89c597d3fb954e4982613d0<SEP>chunk-2e98fa36d7235c33584ec813d1767281", entity_id:"Instruction"}}, {_id:4258, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=207izZBbqVg)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"A meditative concept describing the visualizable space directly in front of closed eyes during contemplation, linked to the \"Namaste\" thought.", created_at:1779259879, source_id:"chunk-2e98fa36d7235c33584ec813d1767281", entity_id:"dark space in front of your closed eyes"}}, {_id:4259, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=207izZBbqVg)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"A separate contemplative statement urging acknowledgment (\"Namaste\") directed at the \"dark space in front of closed eyes.\"", created_at:1779259879, source_id:"chunk-2e98fa36d7235c33584ec813d1767281", entity_id:"Namaste Thought"}}, {_id:4260, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=207izZBbqVg)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Structural issues in the original text including missing punctuation, a typographical period after \"eyes,\" and lack of sentence segmentation.<SEP>The original mantra's lack of punctuation, which makes it a run-on sentence and difficult to read.", created_at:1779259926, source_id:"chunk-2e98fa36d7235c33584ec813d1767281<SEP>chunk-ff94932b6f3b0d226dc634858c45e539", entity_id:"Readability Error"}}, {_id:4261, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=207izZBbqVg)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"A meditative focus object representing the form of a female figure, as referenced in the instructional phrase.", created_at:1779259879, source_id:"chunk-2e98fa36d7235c33584ec813d1767281", entity_id:"her form"}}, {_id:4262, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=207izZBbqVg)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"The punctuation marks added to the mantra to improve readability and structure.", created_at:1779259926, source_id:"chunk-ff94932b6f3b0d226dc634858c45e539", entity_id:"Commas"}}, {_id:4263, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=207izZBbqVg)<SEP>YouTube Video: NJQ573JDmAg (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NJQ573JDmAg)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"The error in interpreting \"a dharana\" as part of the mantra.<SEP>The phenomenon of misinterpreting or mishearing words, discussed in the context of the analyzed phrase.<SEP>Mishearing refers to the possibility that the phrase \"see beyond the physical, even *totally*\" was inaccurately perceived or transcribed from the audio.<SEP>Mishearing refers to the possibility of incorrect auditory interpretation of the phrase in the video.", created_at:1779651910, source_id:"chunk-ff94932b6f3b0d226dc634858c45e539<SEP>chunk-b2829c5543e47705d6bf746f29dc0222<SEP>chunk-071a5d590ca555edd9f20795977f2d3b<SEP>chunk-693990970e9a3acc089ef62a4275e988", entity_id:"Mishearing"}}] AS row
