Miami is a city hosting a program where Sri Preethaji has been present for the last six days. Prieta G is also located in Miami, and the program is taking place there. The descriptions consistently indicate Miami as the setting for the program, with Sri Preethaji's ongoing presence and activities during this period.", source_id:"chunk-d3cae16ffa002440a640f5f63615da00<SEP>chunk-117454b5b8cd20e4fb94422bfd8e3b49<SEP>chunk-49304f84faf57d420319d7f532984c7b", entity_id:"Miami"}}, {_id:4304, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1w-IStuMl3M)", entity_type:"content", truncate:"", description:"A sentence describing seeing a person in a mirror, with facial expressions like smiles and frowns.", created_at:1779261549, source_id:"chunk-1d975f0d94f46d7a04c2a2a43677deb7", entity_id:"When we stand in front of a mirror, we see him in our eyes, in our smiles and frowns."}}, {_id:4305, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1w-IStuMl3M)", entity_type:"content", truncate:"", description:"A sentence about hearing a person in one's own voice when speaking.", created_at:1779261549, source_id:"chunk-1d975f0d94f46d7a04c2a2a43677deb7", entity_id:"When we speak, we hear him in our voice."}}, {_id:4306, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1w-IStuMl3M)<SEP>YouTube Video: idoWVpnJz-Y (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=idoWVpnJz-Y)", entity_type:"person", truncate:"", description:"A person referred to as a biological father, mentioned in the context of flowing through a person.<SEP>Biological father refers to the biological parent who gives life to a child, as recognized in the context of Father's Day celebrations.", created_at:1779401956, source_id:"chunk-1d975f0d94f46d7a04c2a2a43677deb7<SEP>chunk-ed9bd777897b8b08ed12f0776796982a", entity_id:"Biological Father"}}, {_id:4307, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1w-IStuMl3M)", entity_type:"content", truncate:"", description:"A sentence about feeling a person in one's thoughts when emoting.", created_at:1779261549, source_id:"chunk-1d975f0d94f46d7a04c2a2a43677deb7", entity_id:"When we emote, we can feel him in our thoughts."}}, {_id:4308, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1w-IStuMl3M)", entity_type:"content", truncate:"", description:"A sentence about tracing a person in one's gestures through movement.", created_at:1779261549, source_id:"chunk-1d975f0d94f46d7a04c2a2a43677deb7", entity_id:"When we move, we can trace him in our gestures."}}, {_id:4309, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1w-IStuMl3M)", entity_type:"content", truncate:"", description:"A sentence about the presence of a biological father even without meeting them.", created_at:1779261549, source_id:"chunk-1d975f0d94f46d7a04c2a2a43677deb7", entity_id:"Even if you never met your biological father, he still flows through you."}}, {_id:4310, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1w-IStuMl3M)", entity_type:"content", truncate:"", description:"An ancient Hindu chant is referenced in the text, with the speaker explaining its philosophical significance related to honoring fatherly figures.", created_at:1779261625, source_id:"chunk-dc87b4124e027c8ceb12ac0f766b4f97", entity_id:"Ancient Hindu Chant"}}, {_id:4311, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1w-IStuMl3M)", entity_type:"content", truncate:"", description:"This Sanskrit verse is quoted in the text, interpreted as emphasizing the worthiness of five types of individuals as father figures.", created_at:1779261625, source_id:"chunk-dc87b4124e027c8ceb12ac0f766b4f97", entity_id:"Janakascho Paneetha Chha Yascha Vidyam Prayachati"}}, {_id:4312, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1w-IStuMl3M)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"A concept highlighting that five distinct categories of individuals (e.g., biological father, nurturing figures) hold equal significance as fatherly influences.", created_at:1779261625, source_id:"chunk-dc87b4124e027c8ceb12ac0f766b4f97", entity_id:"Five People as Fathers"}}, {_id:4313, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1w-IStuMl3M)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"The provided interpretation defines the chant as honoring five paternal figures: biological father, spiritual initiator, wisdom-giver, sustainer, and liberator from fear.", created_at:1779261649, source_id:"chunk-11e9e2ed6005eca5a1fae0e5e949a2a9", entity_id:"Meaning Explanation"}}, {_id:4314, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1w-IStuMl3M)", entity_type:"content", truncate:"", description:"The Bhagavad Gita is an ancient Indian scripture containing philosophical and spiritual dialogue between Prince Arjuna and the god Krishna.", created_at:1779261649, source_id:"chunk-11e9e2ed6005eca5a1fae0e5e949a2a9", entity_id:"Bhagavad Gita"}}, {_id:4315, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1w-IStuMl3M)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"The garbled verse \"Janakascho paneetha chha yascha vidyam prayachati Anadatha bhyatratha paschaythe pitara smritaha\" represents a transcription error in the chant from the Bhagavad Gita.", created_at:1779261649, source_id:"chunk-11e9e2ed6005eca5a1fae0e5e949a2a9", entity_id:"Garbled Verse Transcription"}}, {_id:4316, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1w-IStuMl3M)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"The definition explains the author's interpretation of the chant as listing five people, separate from the garbled text.<SEP>Defines the concept of five people being worthy of honor as a father.>", created_at:1779261828, source_id:"chunk-c93ac533cca8925d75aa65176000c35b<SEP>chunk-b988235d793b44b746abc1c8a693367b", entity_id:"Definition"}}, {_id:4317, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1w-IStuMl3M)", entity_type:"artifact", truncate:"", description:"A garbled, unreadable segment in the transcription requiring correction to a plausible Sanskrit-ish phrase.<SEP>A repeated phrase \"The one who directed your father\" in the video, identified as a transcription error.<SEP>A garbled chant is mentioned in the text, described as unclear or distorted audio.><SEP>The original chant includes a garbled section with repetitive phrases like \"directed your father.\"", created_at:1779261885, source_id:"chunk-c93ac533cca8925d75aa65176000c35b<SEP>chunk-9eecae952bdf1ea7867999c8da705aa0<SEP>chunk-b988235d793b44b746abc1c8a693367b<SEP>chunk-1439496c0597ca312586a923b138c34d", entity_id:"Garbled Chant"}}, {_id:4318, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1w-IStuMl3M)", entity_type:"content", truncate:"", description:"The author's analysis of the text structure and proposed fixes for the transcription error.", created_at:1779261667, source_id:"chunk-c93ac533cca8925d75aa65176000c35b", entity_id:"Author's Explanation"}}, {_id:4319, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1w-IStuMl3M)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"A plausible linguistic construct suggested for replacing the garbled chant.", created_at:1779261667, source_id:"chunk-c93ac533cca8925d75aa65176000c35b", entity_id:"Sanskrit-ish Phrase"}}] AS row
