UNWIND [{_id:7135, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: QzJ_Ft1de1o (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QzJ_Ft1de1o)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Longevity Genes are genetic traits that enable humans to live longer. According to multiple descriptions, these genetic factors are associated with evolutionary advantages that arise from caring for grandchildren. The traits also support intergenerational support and contribute to species survival. The consistency across the provided descriptions indicates a well-established link between longevity genes and these evolutionary benefits.

The concept of longevity genes highlights how genetic variations can promote extended lifespan, which in turn fosters behaviors that enhance the survival of offspring and grandchildren. This intergenerational support is viewed as an adaptive strategy that benefits the broader species. The repeated emphasis on caring for grandchildren across the descriptions underscores the evolutionary significance of these genetic traits.

The provided descriptions are consistent, indicating a coherent understanding of longevity genes and their evolutionary implications.<SEP>Genetic traits enabling humans to live longer are linked to evolutionary advantages in caring for grandchildren.<SEP>Genetic factors in humans that enable extended lifespan, linked to intergenerational support and species survival.<SEP>Longevity genes are hypothetical biological mechanisms associated with extended lifespan and healthspan.", created_at:1779656853, source_id:"chunk-b2b3f4e0ec4ca323c0c90b860c94bdb5<SEP>chunk-efef91f79f63a3dccc0da4a26bee1fef<SEP>chunk-7438d62acfd111c95d021226c6581819", entity_id:"Longevity Genes"}}, {_id:7136, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: QzJ_Ft1de1o (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QzJ_Ft1de1o)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", created_at:1779656827, description:"Species Survival is the process by which a biological species persists over time. It is maintained through mechanisms such as extended reproductive roles in certain members, which contribute to the species' continuity. Species Survival also involves the continuation of the species via reproduction and the transfer of cultural knowledge across generations. Moreover, it is underpinned by a biological imperative that encourages evolutionary traits, such as extended lifespan, to secure the continuity of life.

The concept of Species Survival encompasses both biological and cultural dimensions. Biologically, it ensures that species reproduce and pass on genetic material, while culturally, knowledge and practices are transmitted, enhancing adaptability. This dual mechanism allows species to respond to environmental changes and maintain resilience. The biological imperative that drives traits like extended lifespan further supports the long-term persistence of species, ensuring that life continues across generations.", source_id:"chunk-efef91f79f63a3dccc0da4a26bee1fef<SEP>chunk-bc3611b977330c3669fa3dd3bfb5860e<SEP>chunk-f8d4df49e2bb59337f3b12dcef1d6f2c", entity_id:"Species Survival"}}, {_id:7137, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source", entity_type:"UNKNOWN", truncate:"", description:"Female killer whales act as grandmothers, supporting younger generations to ensure species survival.", created_at:1779656565, source_id:"chunk-efef91f79f63a3dccc0da4a26bee1fef", entity_id:"Grandmother Role"}}, {_id:7138, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: QzJ_Ft1de1o (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QzJ_Ft1de1o)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Suggestion to replace \"circumference\" with \"consciousness\" in spiritual context for clarity.", created_at:1779656613, source_id:"chunk-cef8de5a4c7a9eb5661ebb0fdc46fa34", entity_id:"Proposed Word Replacement (circumference to consciousness)"}}, {_id:7139, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: QzJ_Ft1de1o (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QzJ_Ft1de1o)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Analysis confirming \"somebody\" as grammatically correct in the context of the prompt.", created_at:1779656613, source_id:"chunk-cef8de5a4c7a9eb5661ebb0fdc46fa34", entity_id:"Grammatical Analysis of 'somebody'"}}, {_id:7140, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: QzJ_Ft1de1o (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QzJ_Ft1de1o)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Analysis confirming \"one's\" as grammatically correct in the context of the prompt.", created_at:1779656613, source_id:"chunk-cef8de5a4c7a9eb5661ebb0fdc46fa34", entity_id:"Grammatical Analysis of 'one's'"}}, {_id:7141, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: QzJ_Ft1de1o (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QzJ_Ft1de1o)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Suggested grammatical correction replacing \"live long\" with \"live a long life\" for improved naturalness.", created_at:1779656699, source_id:"chunk-4f58924914d8390f9a0f22a991598555", entity_id:"Live Long vs Live a Long Life"}}, {_id:7142, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: QzJ_Ft1de1o (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QzJ_Ft1de1o)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Proposed change from \"Let us\" to \"Let's\" for more conversational tone.", created_at:1779656699, source_id:"chunk-4f58924914d8390f9a0f22a991598555", entity_id:"Let Us vs Let's"}}, {_id:7143, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: QzJ_Ft1de1o (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QzJ_Ft1de1o)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Analysis of \"planet\" usage in the context of species existence.", created_at:1779656699, source_id:"chunk-4f58924914d8390f9a0f22a991598555", entity_id:"Planet vs This Planet"}}, {_id:7144, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: QzJ_Ft1de1o (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QzJ_Ft1de1o)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Consideration of alternative terms to \"framework\" for describing biological patterns.", created_at:1779656699, source_id:"chunk-4f58924914d8390f9a0f22a991598555", entity_id:"Framework vs Pattern/Rule"}}, {_id:7145, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: QzJ_Ft1de1o (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QzJ_Ft1de1o)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Discussion of \"reproductive age\" terminology in species survival context.", created_at:1779656699, source_id:"chunk-4f58924914d8390f9a0f22a991598555", entity_id:"Reproductive Age"}}, {_id:7146, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: QzJ_Ft1de1o (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QzJ_Ft1de1o)", entity_type:"creature", truncate:"", description:"Female whales support children and grandchildren after their reproductive age in orca social structures.", created_at:1779656774, source_id:"chunk-335fbb4571ba31c5e62057c887e19129", entity_id:"Female Whales"}}, {_id:7149, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: QzJ_Ft1de1o (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QzJ_Ft1de1o)", entity_type:"creature", truncate:"", description:"Baby whales (including baby killer whales) are highly dependent on their mothers for survival.", created_at:1779656774, source_id:"chunk-335fbb4571ba31c5e62057c887e19129", entity_id:"Baby Whales"}}, {_id:7151, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: QzJ_Ft1de1o (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QzJ_Ft1de1o)", entity_type:"UNKNOWN", truncate:"", description:"Male orcas have a natural lifespan limit of 50 years, after which they die.", created_at:1779656775, source_id:"chunk-335fbb4571ba31c5e62057c887e19129", entity_id:"lifespan"}}, {_id:7152, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: QzJ_Ft1de1o (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QzJ_Ft1de1o)", entity_type:"UNKNOWN", truncate:"", description:"The ocean's harsh conditions directly impact orcas' survival and behavior.", created_at:1779656775, source_id:"chunk-335fbb4571ba31c5e62057c887e19129", entity_id:"life in the ocean"}}, {_id:7153, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: QzJ_Ft1de1o (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QzJ_Ft1de1o)", entity_type:"UNKNOWN", truncate:"", description:"Female whales provide care and support to younger generations post-reproductive age.", created_at:1779656775, source_id:"chunk-335fbb4571ba31c5e62057c887e19129", entity_id:"children and grandchildren"}}, {_id:7154, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: QzJ_Ft1de1o (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QzJ_Ft1de1o)", entity_type:"UNKNOWN", truncate:"", description:"The grandmother whale supports the entire group in overcoming oceanic difficulties.", created_at:1779656775, source_id:"chunk-335fbb4571ba31c5e62057c887e19129", entity_id:"entire group of whales"}}, {_id:7155, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: QzJ_Ft1de1o (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QzJ_Ft1de1o)", entity_type:"UNKNOWN", truncate:"", description:"Orcas rely on salmon as a primary food source for survival and energy.", created_at:1779656775, source_id:"chunk-335fbb4571ba31c5e62057c887e19129", entity_id:"salmon"}}, {_id:7156, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: QzJ_Ft1de1o (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QzJ_Ft1de1o)", entity_type:"artifact", truncate:"", description:"YouTube Video: QzJ_Ft1de1o is a digital video containing commentary on orca behavior and ecological dynamics.<SEP>YouTube Video: QzJ_Ft1de1o is a digital video containing commentary on orca behavior and ecological dynamics.", created_at:1779656790, source_id:"chunk-bc3611b977330c3669fa3dd3bfb5860e", entity_id:"YouTube Video: QzJ_Ft1de1o"}}, {_id:7157, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: QzJ_Ft1de1o (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QzJ_Ft1de1o)", entity_type:"concept", truncate:"", description:"Lifespan of the Male Whale describes the biological limit of male orcas, typically ending at age 50.<SEP>Lifespan of the Male Whale describes the biological limit of male orcas, typically ending at age 50.", created_at:1779656790, source_id:"chunk-bc3611b977330c3669fa3dd3bfb5860e", entity_id:"Lifespan of the Male Whale"}}] AS row
