84: descriptor. 85: This, 86: correction, 87: aims, 88: to, 89: improve, 90: clarity, 91: and, 92: promote, 93: respectful, 94: discourse, 95: around, 96: gender?based, 97: pay, 98: differences.\
\
So about 98 words. That's okay.\
\
Paragraph 2:\
\
\"The original phrase ?paid much lesser than men? is both grammatically awkward and conceptually imprecise. It fails to specify the basis of the comparison and can be perceived as dismissive of the systemic nature of pay gaps. The revised phrase, ?Paid Less Than Men,? provides a straightforward, factual description that aligns with statistical data on gender pay disparities, thereby supporting more accurate communication in academic, policy, and public contexts.\"\
\
