(URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PslFhdZaBFA)", truncate:"", keywords:"consciousness expansion,resonance", weight:1.0, description:"An awake heart?s expanded consciousness field resonates with the loved one?s heart field, initiating healing.", created_at:1779665567, source_id:"chunk-112f236855c8c9ac7864c1e2a1d43d1a"}}, {start: {_id:7425}, end: {_id:7418}, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source", truncate:"", keywords:"conceptual grouping,potential misspelling,thematic continuity,transcription error", weight:4.0, description:"TatTamasee and Tatparamasi are mentioned together in the text, suggesting they are related terms or represent a potential transcription error pair.`<SEP>TatTamasee and Tatparamasi are listed together, suggesting they belong to the same conceptual framework or narrative context.`<SEP>TatTamasee and Tatparamasi are mentioned together in the text, suggesting they are related terms or represent a potential transcription error pair.`<SEP>TatTamasee and Tatparamasi are listed together, suggesting they belong to the same conceptual framework or narrative context.`", created_at:1779665702, source_id:"chunk-11324ba4a521604eab0a83749fcd1adc"}}, {start: {_id:5899}, end: {_id:7422}, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source", truncate:"", keywords:"conceptual substitution,linguistic correction,philosophical relevance,transcription correction", weight:4.0, description:"Massmen is hypothesized to be a transcription error that could be corrected to \"Aham Brahmasmi\" given its thematic relevance to the text's focus on \"I am.\"`<SEP>Massmen is theorized to be a corrupted form of \"Aham Brahmasmi\" given the context of Advaita Vedanta philosophy.`<SEP>Massmen is hypothesized to be a transcription error that could be corrected to \"Aham Brahmasmi\" given its thematic relevance to the text's focus on \"I am.\"`<SEP>Massmen is theorized to be a corrupted form of \"Aham Brahmasmi\" given the context of Advaita Vedanta philosophy.`", created_at:1779665702, source_id