created_at:1779673178, source_id:"chunk-98921940959422839d1d78085fa664be"}}, {start: {_id:7757}, end: {_id:4523}, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Tc8f9ZasRRM)", truncate:"", keywords:"focus area,text improvement", weight:1.0, description:"The core task involved applying grammar corrections to enhance text quality without altering the original meaning or style.", created_at:1779673179, source_id:"chunk-98921940959422839d1d78085fa664be"}}, {start: {_id:2409}, end: {_id:2719}, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Tc8f9ZasRRM)", keywords:"adherence,alignment", truncate:"", weight:1.0, description:"The corrections align with the provided instructions for minimal changes.", created_at:1779673256, source_id:"chunk-1625d2a99ff17f15ce8a139663adfc1b"}}, {start: {_id:2409}, end: {_id:4893}, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Tc8f9ZasRRM)", truncate:"", keywords:"adherence,style preservation", weight:1.0, description:"Corrections are made to maintain the original style without altering the message or tone.", created_at:1779673256, source_id:"chunk-1625d2a99ff17f15ce8a139663adfc1b"}}, {start: {_id:7760}, end: {_id:3471}, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source", keywords:"divine manifestation,transcendence", truncate:"", weight:1.0, description:"Mahasaraswati is invoked during the seventh-ninth nights of Navaratri to transcend Sattva and guide seekers beyond worldly chaos.", created_at:1779673265, source_id:"chunk-7b3a64aa7e92b879d5649be1dd23a938"}}, {start: {_id:7761}, end: {_id:3471}, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jy4hcpUSBms)", keywords:"destruction of darkness,divine form,divine play,religious celebration", truncate:"", weight:2.0, description:"Mahadurga manifests during the first days of Navaratri to overcome Tamas and dark qualities.<SEP>Mahadurga's divine play is part of the Navaratri celebrations.", created_at:1779673404, source_id:"chunk-7b3a64aa7e92b879d5649be1dd23a938<SEP>chunk-0ab03500cfe03bdf3ff37b159be99afe"}}, {start: {_id:7763}, end: {_id:7760}, properties:{file_path:"unknown_source", truncate:"", keywords:"divine vehicle,symbolism,transcendence", weight:3.0, description:"The Himalayan Swan represents the seeker?s transcendental consciousness beyond worldly chaos.<SEP>Mahasaraswati is depicted riding the Himalayan Swan, symbolizing transcendence and unity consciousness.` -> The text says \"rides a Himalayan Swan or Hamsa\". I changed \"or\" to \"and\". The instruction says \"If a single statement describes a relationship involving more than two entities (an N-ary relationship), decompose it into multiple binary (two-entity) relationship pairs for separate description.\" I did this for the swan/hamsa part. The relationship is `Mahasaraswati` and `Himalayan Swan`. The keywords are `symbolism, divine vehicle`. The description is `Mahasaraswati is depicted riding the Himalayan Swan, symbolizing transcendence and unity consciousness.` This seems correct.<SEP>Mahasaraswati is depicted riding the Himalayan Swan, symbolizing transcendence and unity consciousness.` -> Correct.", created_at:1779673265, source_id:"chunk-7b3a64aa7e92b879d5649be1dd23a938<SEP>chunk-06509bca67cf9977473996911215a1e2"}}] AS row
