orms,festival conclusion", weight:1.0, description:"Parashakti is celebrated on the tenth day of Navratri, Vijayadashami, symbolizing the triumph of good over evil.", created_at:1779673523, source_id:"chunk-3d108a7609d2fce897a3df1f09942814"}}, {start: {_id:3470}, end: {_id:7774}, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jy4hcpUSBms)", truncate:"", keywords:"divine forms,festival days", weight:1.0, description:"Mahalakshmi is celebrated during the fourth to sixth days of Navratri, leading to Vijaya Daswami.", created_at:1779673532, source_id:"chunk-3d108a7609d2fce897a3df1f09942814"}}, {start: {_id:904}, end: {_id:7765}, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jy4hcpUSBms)", truncate:"", keywords:"concept,illusion", weight:2.0, description:"Shumba and Nishumba are seen as the third and the final dark forces in mythology, and separation is an illusion.", created_at:1779675421, source_id:"chunk-d333235fcabc3883b17563e023b36fd9"}}, {start: {_id:5540}, end: {_id:7765}, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jy4hcpUSBms)", truncate:"", keywords:"mythology,spiritual concept", weight:2.0, description:"Shumba and Nishumba are seen as the third and the final dark forces in mythology, and Maya is mentioned in the context of going beyond.", created_at:1779675421, source_id:"chunk-d333235fcabc3883b17563e023b36fd9"}}, {start: {_id:7763}, end: {_id:7780}, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jy4hcpUSBms)", keywords:"symbolism,transcendence", truncate:"", weight:1.0, description:"The Himalayan Swan symbolizes the seeker's ability to transcend chaos and attain higher consciousness.", created_at:1779675455, source_id:"chunk-05cc795d538216c463ac6d6e2524a3ee"}}, {start: {_id:7781}, end: {_id:7762}, properties:{file_path:"YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jy4hcpUSBms)", keywords:"mytho